WEBVTT

1
00:00:23.274 --> 00:00:24.608
(GRUNTING)

2
00:00:25.776 --> 00:00:26.777
(WHIRRING)

3
00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:40.791
Whoa!

4
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:42.293
I'm okay.

5
00:00:51.802 --> 00:00:53.804
(ORCHESTRAL MUSIC PLAYING)

6
00:00:56.432 --> 00:00:57.808
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

7
00:01:09.612 --> 00:01:10.988
(BIRD SQUAWKING)

8
00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:19.371
(LITTLE TURTLE
GRUNTING)

9
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.165
(GASPS)

10
00:01:25.878 --> 00:01:26.962
(GROANS)

11
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.217
(GRUNTS)

12
00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.439
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

13
00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:49.026
(MAN SINGING ALONG)

14
00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.615
MAN ON RADIO: <i>Truck 416,
what's your location?</i>

15
00:01:55.324 --> 00:01:59.286
Just passing through a sleepy little
town called Adventure Bay. Over.

16
00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.537
- (BANGING)
- Oh!

17
00:02:00.663 --> 00:02:02.498
(SCREAMS)
That's cold, that's cold!

18
00:02:02.581 --> 00:02:03.666
Oh, ooh, ooh!

19
00:02:03.749 --> 00:02:05.626
I got blue slushie
in my skivvies!

20
00:02:08.003 --> 00:02:09.088
(RUMBLING)

21
00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:10.798
(SQUEALING)

22
00:02:11.715 --> 00:02:13.342
Cold, cold, cold!

23
00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:14.885
(SHRIEKING)

24
00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:16.136
(MOANING)

25
00:02:16.303 --> 00:02:17.388
(GASPS)

26
00:02:17.721 --> 00:02:19.848
Ahhh! Look out, little guy!

27
00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:21.725
(TIRES SCREECHING)

28
00:02:21.809 --> 00:02:22.810
No, no, no, no, no!

29
00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:25.521
Whoa!

30
00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:27.147
Hang in there! Oh, no!

31
00:02:28.232 --> 00:02:29.316
(CLANKING)

32
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.484
Oh, no! No!

33
00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.779
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

34
00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.698
(DRIVER CRIES OUT)

35
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.869
- (TRUCK CREAKING)
- No, no, no!

36
00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:44.540
(SCREAMING)

37
00:02:49.044 --> 00:02:50.879
(SCREAMING)

38
00:02:54.008 --> 00:02:55.634
(HUMMING)

39
00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.094
(GRUNTS)

40
00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.973
DRIVER:
Hello! Down there!

41
00:03:01.056 --> 00:03:03.434
Oh, my. That's not good.

42
00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:05.185
That's not good at all.

43
00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:06.937
Good morning there, friend!

44
00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:10.274
Looks like you're in
a particularly precarious predicament.

45
00:03:10.524 --> 00:03:13.027
Call the police!
Call the fire department!

46
00:03:13.652 --> 00:03:14.903
Call everybody!

47
00:03:15.154 --> 00:03:16.739
You're in Adventure Bay.

48
00:03:16.822 --> 00:03:18.699
Here, we call the PAW Patrol!

49
00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:20.492
You're gonna call the who?

50
00:03:21.702 --> 00:03:23.787
<i>PAW Patrol, PAW Patrol</i>

51
00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:25.873
<i>We'll be there on the double</i>

52
00:03:25.956 --> 00:03:27.750
<i>Whenever there's a problem</i>

53
00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:30.294
<i>Round Adventure Bay</i>

54
00:03:30.377 --> 00:03:32.379
<i>Ryder and his team of pups</i>

55
00:03:32.463 --> 00:03:34.298
<i>Will come and save the day</i>

56
00:03:34.381 --> 00:03:35.883
<i>Marshall, Rubble, Chase</i>

57
00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:37.426
<i>Rocky, Zuma, Skye</i>

58
00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:39.303
<i>Yeah, they're on the way</i>

59
00:03:39.386 --> 00:03:41.180
<i>PAW Patrol, PAW Patrol</i>

60
00:03:41.263 --> 00:03:43.348
<i>Whenever you're in trouble</i>

61
00:03:43.432 --> 00:03:45.559
<i>PAW Patrol, PAW Patrol</i>

62
00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:47.644
<i>We'll be there on the double</i>

63
00:03:47.728 --> 00:03:49.980
<i>No job's too big, no pup's too small</i>

64
00:03:50.064 --> 00:03:52.316
<i>PAW Patrol, we're on a roll!</i>

65
00:03:52.775 --> 00:03:54.735
<i>So here we go
PAW Patrol</i>

66
00:03:54.818 --> 00:03:55.903
<i>Whoa-oh-oh</i>

67
00:03:55.986 --> 00:03:56.987
<i>PAW Patrol</i>

68
00:03:57.071 --> 00:03:58.155
<i>Whoa-oh-oh-oh</i>

69
00:03:58.238 --> 00:03:59.364
<i>PAW Patrol</i>

70
00:04:05.621 --> 00:04:07.331
RYDER ON RADIO:
<i>All right, pups, here we go.</i>

71
00:04:07.414 --> 00:04:09.083
<i>Let's work together out there.</i>

72
00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:13.253
Rocky, I need you to shut down
the bridge and control traffic.

73
00:04:13.587 --> 00:04:14.922
Arf! Flares!

74
00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:16.757
(BEEPING)

75
00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.467
(CLINKING)

76
00:04:21.845 --> 00:04:24.765
Zuma, I need you to keep
that waterway clear.

77
00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.350
Nobody under the bridge.

78
00:04:26.892 --> 00:04:28.310
ZUMA: You got it, Ryder!

79
00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:30.479
- Waterway secure!
- (BEEPING)

80
00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.356
(TIRES SCREECH)

81
00:04:32.439 --> 00:04:34.691
Chase, it's all up to you.

82
00:04:34.775 --> 00:04:37.861
Use the winch in your pup pack to get
the driver and bring him to safety!

83
00:04:38.237 --> 00:04:39.905
Chase is on the case!

84
00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:46.411
Arf! Grappling hook!

85
00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:52.084
(HOWLING)

86
00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:56.880
Sir, don't be alarmed.
I'm coming down!

87
00:04:56.964 --> 00:04:59.967
Oh, thank you, thank you,
thank you, the rescue team is here!

88
00:05:01.885 --> 00:05:03.470
A dog?

89
00:05:03.554 --> 00:05:05.931
Actually, sir, I'm a puppy.

90
00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.475
A baby dog?
That's even worse!

91
00:05:08.559 --> 00:05:11.061
You're in shock, so I'm not
going to take that personally.

92
00:05:11.145 --> 00:05:12.896
Now, let's get you out of here.

93
00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:16.066
No way! I'm waiting
right here for a real rescue.

94
00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.442
- (BANGING)
- Ahhh!

95
00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:19.403
I changed my mind,
I'll go with you!

96
00:05:19.862 --> 00:05:22.865
Ryder! These cables
aren't going to hold much longer!

97
00:05:22.948 --> 00:05:25.033
Let's go, Chase.
Get him out of there!

98
00:05:25.117 --> 00:05:26.577
CHASE: We're coming out!

99
00:05:27.119 --> 00:05:28.662
Oh! Oh!

100
00:05:28.745 --> 00:05:31.373
Don't panic.
I need you to stay calm.

101
00:05:32.207 --> 00:05:34.084
No deal! I'm freaking out!

102
00:05:34.168 --> 00:05:36.336
Then you're really
not going to like this!

103
00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.338
Ahhh!

104
00:05:38.505 --> 00:05:41.383
We're not going to make it.
We're not going to make it!

105
00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.052
Ah!

106
00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.430
You can open your eyes now.

107
00:05:47.514 --> 00:05:49.057
Oh, we made it. (LAUGHING)

108
00:05:49.141 --> 00:05:50.225
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

109
00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:52.644
Great work, PAW Patrol!

110
00:05:52.811 --> 00:05:53.854
(ROOSTER CROWING)

111
00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:55.439
Everybody get back!

112
00:05:55.522 --> 00:05:57.274
- The truck's leaking gas!
- (PEOPLE GASPING)

113
00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:00.861
Oh, come on, that's not gas.

114
00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:02.946
That's the stuff I've been
hauling from coast to coast.

115
00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.532
That is pure Canadian maple syrup!

116
00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:08.076
Okay, time to clean up this mess.

117
00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.330
Deploy waffles, pancakes,
and French toast!

118
00:06:11.538 --> 00:06:13.248
(LAUGHING)

119
00:06:14.708 --> 00:06:15.792
(WHIMPERING)

120
00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:20.047
It's okay, little guy, you're safe.

121
00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.590
You can come out now.

122
00:06:21.673 --> 00:06:22.758
(SQUEALING)

123
00:06:22.841 --> 00:06:24.885
Let's get you back to your family.

124
00:06:32.684 --> 00:06:33.769
(SQUEALING)

125
00:06:35.479 --> 00:06:36.772
There you go.

126
00:06:36.855 --> 00:06:37.898
(SQUEALING)

127
00:06:38.982 --> 00:06:40.234
Great work, pups.

128
00:06:40.317 --> 00:06:41.860
Another perfect rescue.

129
00:06:41.944 --> 00:06:43.946
(HOWLING)

130
00:06:45.739 --> 00:06:47.241
(RHYTHMIC MUSIC PLAYING)

131
00:06:53.497 --> 00:06:56.833
<i>I woke up this morning
And I took a look outside</i>

132
00:06:56.917 --> 00:06:59.628
<i>And I was like
Oh, yeah, oh, yeah</i>

133
00:06:59.711 --> 00:07:00.963
Oh! Um...

134
00:07:01.171 --> 00:07:02.714
Hey. Excuse me?

135
00:07:03.131 --> 00:07:04.424
You dropped something.

136
00:07:05.259 --> 00:07:06.635
I'm done with it.

137
00:07:06.885 --> 00:07:08.804
Buzz off, wiener dog.

138
00:07:09.263 --> 00:07:10.305
"Wiener dog"?

139
00:07:10.764 --> 00:07:13.183
Maybe you should just pick that up
and put it in the trash!

140
00:07:13.392 --> 00:07:14.643
(LAUGHING)

141
00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:16.311
Yeah? Or what?

142
00:07:16.395 --> 00:07:19.314
Or I'm going to pick you up
and put you in the trash.

143
00:07:19.398 --> 00:07:20.440
(PEOPLE GASPING)

144
00:07:21.233 --> 00:07:22.818
Hey, I don't want no trouble.

145
00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:25.612
I'm pickin' up the trash,
I'm pickin' up the trash.

146
00:07:26.113 --> 00:07:28.949
Thank you. We've all got
to take pride in our city.

147
00:07:29.032 --> 00:07:30.033
Don't ever forget that.

148
00:07:30.117 --> 00:07:31.285
MAN OVER PA:
<i>This is the D train...</i>

149
00:07:31.368 --> 00:07:33.954
This is my stop. It's been a slice.

150
00:07:35.831 --> 00:07:38.000
I'm going to turn my life around.
I really am.

151
00:07:39.751 --> 00:07:42.587
<i>I've got a real good feeling</i>

152
00:07:42.963 --> 00:07:44.673
Hey, Liberty!

153
00:07:44.756 --> 00:07:46.008
<i>I've got a real good feeling</i>

154
00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:48.218
<i>That we're doing something right</i>

155
00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.435
It's election day in Adventure City.

156
00:07:56.518 --> 00:07:59.730
I'm Marty Muckraker,
reporting live from City Square.

157
00:07:59.813 --> 00:08:02.274
<i>In a surprising twist,
the leading candidate</i>

158
00:08:02.357 --> 00:08:03.692
<i>has dropped out of the race,</i>

159
00:08:03.775 --> 00:08:05.527
<i>leaving only one name
on the ticket.</i>

160
00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:09.197
<i>Mayor Humdinger,
who has just won by default.</i>

161
00:08:09.531 --> 00:08:11.033
Mayor Humdinger.

162
00:08:11.116 --> 00:08:12.200
Ugh!

163
00:08:12.284 --> 00:08:13.910
Just saying it makes my skin crawl.

164
00:08:14.661 --> 00:08:15.871
No dogs.

165
00:08:15.954 --> 00:08:17.289
By order of the new mayor.

166
00:08:17.372 --> 00:08:19.916
- Excuse me?
- Yeah, you heard him.

167
00:08:20.042 --> 00:08:21.126
No dogs.

168
00:08:24.129 --> 00:08:25.714
He's more of a cat person.

169
00:08:25.797 --> 00:08:27.090
Now beat it!

170
00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:30.135
If those are the rules,
those are the rules.

171
00:08:30.218 --> 00:08:33.388
(LAUGHING)
You gentlemen have a wonderful day.

172
00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:35.182
Ha-ha! Did you see that?

173
00:08:35.265 --> 00:08:37.809
You gotta show
these dogs you're the alpha.

174
00:08:37.893 --> 00:08:40.479
You're not the alpha.
I'm the alpha!

175
00:08:40.562 --> 00:08:42.981
- No, I'm the alpha!
- No, I'm the alpha!

176
00:08:43.065 --> 00:08:44.524
I'm the
alpha!

177
00:08:44.608 --> 00:08:45.859
(GROANING)

178
00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:48.779
Right this way, ma'am.

179
00:08:50.238 --> 00:08:52.491
- I'm the alpha!
- No. I'm the alpha!

180
00:08:52.574 --> 00:08:53.575
(GROANING)

181
00:08:55.827 --> 00:08:58.080
- Thanks for the lift!
- WOMAN: Happy to help.

182
00:08:58.455 --> 00:09:00.165
Excuse me, coming through,

183
00:09:00.248 --> 00:09:02.584
make way, pardon me, underfoot.

184
00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:05.670
MAN: <i>Please welcome to the stage,</i>

185
00:09:05.754 --> 00:09:08.465
<i>a man who needs no introduction.</i>

186
00:09:08.548 --> 00:09:12.094
<i>He's literally the greatest
human being on the planet.</i>

187
00:09:12.177 --> 00:09:15.013
<i>He's... Me!</i>

188
00:09:15.639 --> 00:09:17.265
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

189
00:09:23.063 --> 00:09:24.272
(COUGHING)

190
00:09:29.236 --> 00:09:32.656
<i>I am the champion</i>

191
00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:34.866
<i>Thank you, thank you.</i>

192
00:09:34.991 --> 00:09:35.992
(PARTY HORN BLOWING)

193
00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:38.995
- Really?
- Yeah...

194
00:09:39.079 --> 00:09:40.497
<i>I want to start off by thanking</i>

195
00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.707
<i>each and every one of you
for choosing me</i>

196
00:09:42.833 --> 00:09:44.459
<i>to be your new mayor.</i>

197
00:09:44.543 --> 00:09:46.962
You were the only name on the ballot!

198
00:09:47.379 --> 00:09:50.173
<i>You could only vote for one
name anyway, so what does it matter?</i>

199
00:09:50.257 --> 00:09:52.968
<i>I won this election fair and square.</i>

200
00:09:53.343 --> 00:09:56.596
Well, maybe not fair,
but who's keeping track?

201
00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:57.764
(LAUGHING)

202
00:09:58.098 --> 00:10:00.809
<i>You know, they call this place
Adventure City,</i>

203
00:10:00.892 --> 00:10:03.311
<i>but what's so adventure-y about it?</i>

204
00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:06.022
<i>The truth is, it's boring.</i>

205
00:10:06.231 --> 00:10:08.442
<i>Libraries? Boring!</i>

206
00:10:08.525 --> 00:10:09.568
- (MEOWS)
- (CRASHING)

207
00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:12.112
<i>Museums? Boring!</i>

208
00:10:12.404 --> 00:10:13.488
- (CROWD MURMURING)
- (CRASHING)

209
00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:15.615
<i>Cute little dog parks?</i>

210
00:10:15.699 --> 00:10:16.992
ALL: Aw.

211
00:10:17.617 --> 00:10:19.369
<i>Ugh! Definitely boring!</i>

212
00:10:19.453 --> 00:10:20.579
(CROWD GASPING)

213
00:10:20.787 --> 00:10:21.830
<i>But don't worry.</i>

214
00:10:21.913 --> 00:10:25.750
<i>I'm going to put the adventure
back in Adventure City!</i>

215
00:10:25.834 --> 00:10:30.338
<i>When I'm done with this place,
you won't even recognize it.</i>

216
00:10:30.505 --> 00:10:32.132
(LAUGHING)

217
00:10:32.382 --> 00:10:33.467
(GASPS)

218
00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:34.593
(GROANS)

219
00:10:35.385 --> 00:10:36.511
(PHONE RINGING)

220
00:10:39.097 --> 00:10:41.057
PAW Patrol.
What's your emergency?

221
00:10:41.141 --> 00:10:43.977
<i>What? You answer your own calls?</i>

222
00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.855
<i>Oh, my goodness,
I didn't even think I was gonna...</i>

223
00:10:46.938 --> 00:10:48.315
<i>Oh!</i>

224
00:10:48.523 --> 00:10:51.776
<i>I can't believe
I'm looking at the PAW Patrol!</i>

225
00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.613
<i>I am such a big fan!
This is off the leash!</i>

226
00:10:54.905 --> 00:10:57.532
Is there something
we can help you with?

227
00:10:57.616 --> 00:10:59.701
<i>Yes, yes, yes!</i>

228
00:10:59.784 --> 00:11:02.621
<i>My name is Liberty,
and I'm calling from Adventure City.</i>

229
00:11:02.704 --> 00:11:04.456
<i>Something terrible has happened.</i>

230
00:11:04.539 --> 00:11:07.459
<i>Humdinger was just elected mayor.</i>

231
00:11:07.542 --> 00:11:09.252
ALL: Humdinger?

232
00:11:09.336 --> 00:11:11.922
He's the worst mayor
in the history of mayors!

233
00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:14.007
And that's being generous.

234
00:11:14.341 --> 00:11:16.801
<i>You're telling me,
this guy's a disaster!</i>

235
00:11:16.885 --> 00:11:19.137
<i>He's going to destroy the whole city.</i>

236
00:11:19.221 --> 00:11:20.639
<i>Please, we need your help.</i>

237
00:11:20.722 --> 00:11:21.723
<i>Come quickly!</i>

238
00:11:22.891 --> 00:11:24.518
Adventure City's in trouble.

239
00:11:24.601 --> 00:11:26.520
Come on, pups, pack your things.

240
00:11:26.603 --> 00:11:29.314
No city's too big,
no pup's too small!

241
00:11:29.397 --> 00:11:30.482
(BARKING AND HOWLING)

242
00:11:30.565 --> 00:11:32.025
Yeah!

243
00:11:32.442 --> 00:11:33.443
What's wrong, Chase?

244
00:11:33.902 --> 00:11:34.945
I'm not going.

245
00:11:35.403 --> 00:11:37.697
We have to go. They need us.

246
00:11:37.781 --> 00:11:40.075
I'm never going back to Adventure City!

247
00:11:41.284 --> 00:11:42.369
Chase...

248
00:11:42.911 --> 00:11:44.579
What's got his leash in a knot?

249
00:11:45.288 --> 00:11:48.333
Chase has a history
with Adventure City.

250
00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.461
He has a lot of tough memories
from that place.

251
00:11:53.922 --> 00:11:55.799
<i>He was abandoned there as a pup.</i>

252
00:12:01.054 --> 00:12:04.057
<i>The city was so big,
and he was so small.</i>

253
00:12:05.892 --> 00:12:06.977
(CARS HONKING)

254
00:12:07.185 --> 00:12:08.270
(PANTING)

255
00:12:09.604 --> 00:12:11.064
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

256
00:12:11.356 --> 00:12:13.024
<i>It was a hard life.</i>

257
00:12:13.358 --> 00:12:14.359
(GRUNTS)

258
00:12:16.111 --> 00:12:17.237
(HONKING)

259
00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.155
- (GASPS)
- (TIRES SCREECHING)

260
00:12:20.907 --> 00:12:23.910
The city can be a scary place
when you're all alone.

261
00:12:24.202 --> 00:12:26.746
- Is that where you found him?
- That's right.

262
00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.666
And I brought him back here
to Adventure Bay.

263
00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.503
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

264
00:12:36.006 --> 00:12:37.382
Chase?

265
00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:39.634
Let's talk about this.

266
00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:43.013
I don't want to go back to
Adventure City.

267
00:12:43.263 --> 00:12:46.266
I know it was tough,
but that was a long time ago.

268
00:12:46.933 --> 00:12:48.685
I'm afraid if I go back there,

269
00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.521
everyone will see
I'm still that scared little puppy,

270
00:12:51.813 --> 00:12:54.024
and not the hero they think I am.

271
00:12:54.524 --> 00:12:57.777
I promise it will be nothing like
it was when you were little.

272
00:12:57.902 --> 00:12:59.487
Everything will be fine.

273
00:13:00.155 --> 00:13:02.699
Come on, Chase.
Those people need our help.

274
00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:05.535
We're the PAW Patrol,
this is what we do.

275
00:13:06.077 --> 00:13:07.078
Trust me.

276
00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.459
Okay. I trust you.

277
00:13:12.959 --> 00:13:15.045
Now, can I get a yelp?

278
00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:16.588
(HOWLS SOFTLY)

279
00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.633
Come on. You can do
better than that.

280
00:13:20.592 --> 00:13:22.427
(HOWLING EMPHATICALLY)

281
00:13:22.677 --> 00:13:24.721
Attaboy! Let's get to work.

282
00:13:28.016 --> 00:13:32.520
Skye, Chase, Rocky,
Marshall, Zuma...

283
00:13:33.188 --> 00:13:34.564
(METAL CREAKING)

284
00:13:35.023 --> 00:13:36.524
Rubble!

285
00:13:37.067 --> 00:13:40.278
It's not my fault!
I couldn't decide what to bring.

286
00:13:40.362 --> 00:13:42.155
So I brought everything!

287
00:13:42.572 --> 00:13:43.698
(GRUNTING)

288
00:13:46.618 --> 00:13:50.747
Get there, come on.
Come on, come on!

289
00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:53.708
See? It fits!

290
00:13:53.958 --> 00:13:55.043
(SIGHING)

291
00:13:55.794 --> 00:13:57.295
(RHYTHMIC MUSIC PLAYING)

292
00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:01.424
PAW Patrol is on a roll!

293
00:14:01.508 --> 00:14:03.009
ALL: Road trip! (HOWLING)

294
00:14:03.426 --> 00:14:06.971
<i>Hop in my ride
Don't you know</i>

295
00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:11.017
<i>We got the sun
Always shining wherever we go</i>

296
00:14:11.101 --> 00:14:15.271
<i>Don't need no map
We just roll</i>

297
00:14:15.397 --> 00:14:19.067
<i>Let the vibe give direction
Take control</i>

298
00:14:19.192 --> 00:14:20.819
<i>When it's good
When it's bad</i>

299
00:14:20.902 --> 00:14:22.946
<i>Yeah, you got me</i>

300
00:14:23.029 --> 00:14:26.199
<i>And when I turn around</i>

301
00:14:26.282 --> 00:14:27.867
- Hi!
- Hi!

302
00:14:28.493 --> 00:14:32.038
<i>You got a way to make
a problem disappear</i>

303
00:14:32.122 --> 00:14:33.123
<i>Up to the clouds</i>

304
00:14:33.289 --> 00:14:34.416
(LAUGHING) Bye!

305
00:14:34.541 --> 00:14:36.209
<i>I'm spinning around</i>

306
00:14:36.292 --> 00:14:38.044
<i>And now you know why</i>

307
00:14:39.129 --> 00:14:42.799
<i>'Cause no one in this world
Can make me feel loved</i>

308
00:14:42.882 --> 00:14:46.845
<i>In the way that you do now</i>

309
00:14:47.011 --> 00:14:50.724
<i>No, no one in this world
can make me come down</i>

310
00:14:50.807 --> 00:14:54.769
<i>-When I'm in such a good mood now</i>
-(GRUNTS)

311
00:14:56.479 --> 00:14:57.772
<i>Yeah</i>

312
00:14:59.649 --> 00:15:00.775
(GASPS)

313
00:15:04.696 --> 00:15:05.697
(SNORING)

314
00:15:06.823 --> 00:15:08.199
<i>Good mood</i>

315
00:15:09.367 --> 00:15:10.452
(SNORING)

316
00:15:10.618 --> 00:15:11.995
<i>-Good mood</i>
-(GROANS)

317
00:15:13.997 --> 00:15:15.582
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

318
00:15:16.458 --> 00:15:17.792
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

319
00:15:20.336 --> 00:15:22.005
Wake up, pups, we're here!

320
00:15:22.881 --> 00:15:24.090
(GASPS) Oh, wow!

321
00:15:24.174 --> 00:15:25.175
- Check it out!
- Cool!

322
00:15:25.258 --> 00:15:27.844
- No way!
- It's amazing!

323
00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:31.139
SKYE: This place
is so much bigger than Adventure Bay.

324
00:15:34.517 --> 00:15:35.852
You okay, Chase?

325
00:15:36.436 --> 00:15:39.230
It's a lot bigger than I remember.

326
00:15:42.025 --> 00:15:44.486
It's like they super-sized it!

327
00:15:44.611 --> 00:15:45.820
(RAIN POURING)

328
00:15:48.323 --> 00:15:49.324
(CAR HONKING)

329
00:15:54.496 --> 00:15:56.080
HUMDINGER: Ugh! Rain!

330
00:15:56.164 --> 00:15:59.125
Does it always rain in this lousy city?

331
00:16:00.043 --> 00:16:01.377
(THUNDER CRASHING)

332
00:16:03.838 --> 00:16:05.006
(GASPS)

333
00:16:05.215 --> 00:16:06.299
(MEOWING)

334
00:16:06.633 --> 00:16:07.634
(CUP BREAKING)

335
00:16:08.426 --> 00:16:11.221
Okay, which one of you
eggheads is in charge?

336
00:16:11.346 --> 00:16:12.388
- Hello!
- Gah!

337
00:16:13.056 --> 00:16:15.350
I'm the lead egghead.
Kendra Wilson.

338
00:16:15.683 --> 00:16:16.768
Hmm.

339
00:16:16.851 --> 00:16:18.686
I've got a fireworks
celebration tonight

340
00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:21.189
and they're going
to cancel it because of the rain.

341
00:16:21.272 --> 00:16:25.068
I hear you have a weather machine
that sucks up clouds.

342
00:16:25.151 --> 00:16:26.277
Is that true?

343
00:16:26.611 --> 00:16:27.987
You're looking at it.

344
00:16:28.071 --> 00:16:30.073
It's a free-floating
gyroscopically balanced

345
00:16:30.156 --> 00:16:33.034
remote-controlled weather containment
and analysis apparatus.

346
00:16:33.493 --> 00:16:36.663
What? I don't understand
a word you just said.

347
00:16:37.372 --> 00:16:38.373
Well... (LAUGHS)

348
00:16:38.456 --> 00:16:39.999
We call it the Cloud Catcher.

349
00:16:40.083 --> 00:16:41.960
It flies around
and sucks up clouds,

350
00:16:42.043 --> 00:16:45.004
then brings them
back to the lab so we can study them.

351
00:16:45.088 --> 00:16:46.256
Excellent, excellent.

352
00:16:46.339 --> 00:16:50.218
Well, kitties, it looks
like our bad weather problem is solved.

353
00:16:50.468 --> 00:16:53.179
I want all those pesky rain clouds
sucked up by the end of the day.

354
00:16:53.763 --> 00:16:56.558
Oh! I'm sorry if I wasn't clear.

355
00:16:56.641 --> 00:16:59.018
The Cloud Catcher is for
studying clouds,

356
00:16:59.102 --> 00:17:00.728
not for changing the weather.

357
00:17:00.812 --> 00:17:03.523
And I'm sorry if I wasn't clear.

358
00:17:03.606 --> 00:17:07.193
Suck up those clouds
or I'm closing this university forever!

359
00:17:07.277 --> 00:17:08.528
(PEOPLE GASPING)

360
00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.113
Well...

361
00:17:10.196 --> 00:17:14.117
I guess we could
try using it to clear the rain clouds.

362
00:17:14.659 --> 00:17:16.703
- Just for tonight.
- Wonderful!

363
00:17:16.786 --> 00:17:20.164
That's what I call scientific consensus!

364
00:17:21.165 --> 00:17:22.375
(WHIRRING)

365
00:17:24.752 --> 00:17:26.004
(MEOWING)

366
00:17:30.425 --> 00:17:31.843
(BEEPING)

367
00:17:35.305 --> 00:17:36.431
Oh!

368
00:17:37.473 --> 00:17:38.808
My top hat!

369
00:17:38.892 --> 00:17:40.351
Here you go, boss.

370
00:17:42.437 --> 00:17:43.563
(MACHINE BEEPING)

371
00:17:43.771 --> 00:17:44.939
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

372
00:17:55.074 --> 00:17:56.618
(WHIRRING)

373
00:18:00.955 --> 00:18:02.957
That's incredible!

374
00:18:03.082 --> 00:18:05.084
(LAUGHING AND SINGING JOYFULLY)

375
00:18:06.461 --> 00:18:09.172
We'll have the sky
clear by sundown.

376
00:18:09.255 --> 00:18:12.008
Ugh! I've got a bad feeling about this.

377
00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:13.676
- I'll hang on to this remote!
- (GASPS)

378
00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:15.845
People are going
to love these fireworks,

379
00:18:15.929 --> 00:18:19.390
and more importantly,
they're going to love me!

380
00:18:23.269 --> 00:18:24.437
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

381
00:18:27.273 --> 00:18:29.859
All right, pups, keep an eye out for
the new headquarters.

382
00:18:29.943 --> 00:18:31.277
- We're almost there.
- Yeah!

383
00:18:31.361 --> 00:18:33.529
- Cool!
- I can't wait!

384
00:18:33.613 --> 00:18:36.032
- Where is it?
- There's so many buildings!

385
00:18:36.115 --> 00:18:37.742
I wonder which one it is.

386
00:18:40.119 --> 00:18:41.412
ALL: Whoa!

387
00:18:41.746 --> 00:18:42.830
RYDER: Oh. (CHUCKLING)

388
00:18:42.914 --> 00:18:44.707
Yeah. Couldn't have missed that.

389
00:18:45.583 --> 00:18:47.210
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

390
00:19:06.562 --> 00:19:07.855
ALL: Whoa!

391
00:19:07.939 --> 00:19:11.651
Welcome to our new
Adventure City headquarters.

392
00:19:11.734 --> 00:19:13.111
- Whoa!
- Wow!

393
00:19:13.277 --> 00:19:14.278
Awesome!

394
00:19:14.362 --> 00:19:15.697
ROCKY: Now, that's a view!

395
00:19:15.863 --> 00:19:16.948
Whoa!

396
00:19:17.573 --> 00:19:19.492
How can we afford this place?

397
00:19:20.201 --> 00:19:22.537
Officially licensed
PAW Patrol merchandise.

398
00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:24.455
This stuff sells like hot cakes!

399
00:19:24.539 --> 00:19:25.623
(BEEPING)

400
00:19:25.707 --> 00:19:27.959
We've got everything we need
at our fingertips.

401
00:19:29.002 --> 00:19:30.211
Ahhh! (GRUNTS)

402
00:19:30.294 --> 00:19:31.295
(PUPS LAUGHING)

403
00:19:31.379 --> 00:19:32.630
- Marshall!
- Marshall!

404
00:19:32.755 --> 00:19:35.758
Next time, warn me
before you stick a building up my nose!

405
00:19:35.925 --> 00:19:36.968
(LAUGHING)

406
00:19:37.218 --> 00:19:39.095
This is so cool!

407
00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:40.763
It's so high-tech!

408
00:19:41.597 --> 00:19:42.932
And check this out.

409
00:19:43.016 --> 00:19:45.893
There's even
a new and improved pup treat dispenser.

410
00:19:46.102 --> 00:19:47.645
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

411
00:19:48.021 --> 00:19:52.567
(SINGING A HIGH NOTE)

412
00:19:53.026 --> 00:19:54.736
(LAUGHING)

413
00:19:54.819 --> 00:19:57.238
What? It's a beautiful thing.

414
00:19:58.364 --> 00:20:01.159
Last but not least,
this is our mission prep area.

415
00:20:01.367 --> 00:20:03.453
Everybody's got their own cubby.

416
00:20:03.953 --> 00:20:05.496
Oh, oh, oh! I want that one!

417
00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:07.331
RYDER: No, Rubble, don't!
That cubby belongs to...

418
00:20:07.749 --> 00:20:09.042
- (WHIRRING)
- (RUBBLE GRUNTS)

419
00:20:10.251 --> 00:20:11.544
- AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Skye!</i>
- (GRUNTS)

420
00:20:13.588 --> 00:20:14.922
...Skye.

421
00:20:15.715 --> 00:20:16.758
Oops.

422
00:20:16.841 --> 00:20:20.386
It's not important how it looks,
it's how it makes you feel.

423
00:20:20.678 --> 00:20:23.723
I think you guys are going to have
to cut me out of this thing.

424
00:20:25.058 --> 00:20:26.142
(ALL LAUGHING)

425
00:20:26.225 --> 00:20:27.852
Actually, I'm good.

426
00:20:29.687 --> 00:20:30.688
(BEEPING)

427
00:20:30.772 --> 00:20:32.023
(WHIRRING)

428
00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:34.025
(DINGING)

429
00:20:40.698 --> 00:20:43.326
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
I've gathered you here tonight</i>

430
00:20:43.409 --> 00:20:45.536
<i>for a very important reason.</i>

431
00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:47.205
<i>To celebrate me!</i>

432
00:20:48.498 --> 00:20:50.374
<i>Prepare to be blown away</i>

433
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:54.504
<i>by the most breathtaking
fireworks display you've ever seen!</i>

434
00:20:54.587 --> 00:20:58.549
<i>Time to light up the sky!</i>

435
00:20:58.633 --> 00:20:59.884
(WHIZZING)

436
00:21:01.094 --> 00:21:02.095
(FIREWORK POPS SOFTLY)

437
00:21:02.178 --> 00:21:03.179
(CROWD SIGHING
IN DISAPPOINTMENT)

438
00:21:06.015 --> 00:21:07.100
(WHIZZING)

439
00:21:08.267 --> 00:21:09.352
(POPS SOFTLY)

440
00:21:09.435 --> 00:21:10.645
(CROWD SIGHING)

441
00:21:11.104 --> 00:21:14.315
Yeesh! This is less
than spectacular.

442
00:21:14.398 --> 00:21:15.775
You, ponytail man!

443
00:21:15.858 --> 00:21:18.152
Why are you taking so long
between fireworks?

444
00:21:18.236 --> 00:21:20.196
I'm building momentum, man.

445
00:21:20.279 --> 00:21:23.032
I have a whole routine
mapped out in my head.

446
00:21:23.116 --> 00:21:25.034
Nobody's got time for
your self-indulgent,

447
00:21:25.118 --> 00:21:26.661
hippy-dippy art project.

448
00:21:26.744 --> 00:21:28.538
They want spectacle!

449
00:21:28.621 --> 00:21:29.831
(WHIRRING AND BEEPING)

450
00:21:30.873 --> 00:21:32.166
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

451
00:21:33.668 --> 00:21:34.961
(CRACKLING)

452
00:21:36.045 --> 00:21:37.088
(LAUGHING)

453
00:21:37.672 --> 00:21:38.798
(CRACKLING)

454
00:21:39.924 --> 00:21:42.718
Rock and roll, man!

455
00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:44.345
(CROWD GASPING IN AWE)

456
00:21:46.139 --> 00:21:48.182
- (CHEERING)
- Yay!

457
00:21:48.266 --> 00:21:49.767
They're all for me!

458
00:21:55.898 --> 00:21:57.066
(MEOWING)

459
00:21:57.733 --> 00:21:58.818
(GASPS)

460
00:22:01.279 --> 00:22:02.280
(CRACKING)

461
00:22:04.907 --> 00:22:06.033
Ahhh!

462
00:22:06.117 --> 00:22:07.160
Oh, boy!

463
00:22:07.243 --> 00:22:08.452
Whoa!

464
00:22:08.619 --> 00:22:09.954
(ALL SCREAMING)

465
00:22:10.246 --> 00:22:12.081
Oh! Wow!

466
00:22:12.165 --> 00:22:15.209
How often do you get to see
fireworks this close?

467
00:22:16.502 --> 00:22:17.920
My top hat!

468
00:22:18.004 --> 00:22:19.505
- Here you go, boss!
- Ahhh!

469
00:22:21.674 --> 00:22:22.758
(GRUNTING)

470
00:22:23.092 --> 00:22:25.553
This is why dogs hate fireworks!

471
00:22:28.681 --> 00:22:30.141
Whoa...

472
00:22:31.642 --> 00:22:33.936
(FIREWORKS EXPLODING IN THE DISTANCE)

473
00:22:36.856 --> 00:22:38.441
I'm no expert,

474
00:22:38.524 --> 00:22:42.028
but aren't fireworks supposed
to explode in the sky?

475
00:22:43.362 --> 00:22:44.864
Let's see what's going on!

476
00:22:46.699 --> 00:22:49.368
It looks like Mayor Humdinger's
fireworks display

477
00:22:49.452 --> 00:22:51.954
has turned into a fireworks disaster.

478
00:22:52.038 --> 00:22:55.416
We've got to stop those fireworks
before they burn down the city.

479
00:22:55.666 --> 00:22:57.001
Time to suit up!

480
00:22:58.502 --> 00:23:00.588
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

481
00:23:25.821 --> 00:23:27.031
(GROWLING)

482
00:23:28.991 --> 00:23:30.076
Whoa!

483
00:23:40.211 --> 00:23:41.671
Thanks, robot arm!

484
00:23:42.505 --> 00:23:45.258
PAW Patrol, ready for action, Ryder sir!

485
00:23:47.802 --> 00:23:48.844
(BEEPING)

486
00:23:49.345 --> 00:23:50.930
(CREAKING)

487
00:23:54.809 --> 00:23:56.143
(BEEPING)

488
00:23:59.814 --> 00:24:01.023
(GASPING)

489
00:24:02.024 --> 00:24:03.234
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

490
00:24:24.171 --> 00:24:25.339
PUPS: Whoa!

491
00:24:27.842 --> 00:24:30.386
RYDER: This is your new car.

492
00:24:30.761 --> 00:24:31.846
Wow!

493
00:24:31.929 --> 00:24:33.139
Awesome!

494
00:24:40.271 --> 00:24:41.897
(HOWLING)

495
00:24:44.233 --> 00:24:45.985
(BEEPING)

496
00:24:46.277 --> 00:24:47.570
So cool!

497
00:24:49.196 --> 00:24:50.531
(ENGINE STARTING)

498
00:24:55.703 --> 00:24:57.496
I could get used to this.

499
00:24:58.205 --> 00:24:59.999
You better hang on to your hat.

500
00:25:00.624 --> 00:25:03.627
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Chase!
Ready for launch in five...</i>

501
00:25:04.253 --> 00:25:09.383
<i>- Four... Three... Two... One.</i>
- (TIRES SCREECHING)

502
00:25:09.633 --> 00:25:10.634
<i>Go!</i>

503
00:25:10.885 --> 00:25:12.762
- (HORN SOUNDING)
- (TIRES SCREECHING)

504
00:25:13.179 --> 00:25:14.764
<i>PAW Patrol</i>

505
00:25:14.847 --> 00:25:15.931
(HOWLING)

506
00:25:16.015 --> 00:25:17.600
<i>Go, go, go, go, go</i>

507
00:25:17.683 --> 00:25:19.393
<i>Go, PAW Patrol</i>

508
00:25:20.019 --> 00:25:22.229
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Marshall. Go!</i>

509
00:25:24.065 --> 00:25:25.399
(SIREN BLARING)

510
00:25:31.864 --> 00:25:33.949
<i>Go, go, go, go, go</i>

511
00:25:34.033 --> 00:25:35.368
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Skye.</i>

512
00:25:35.451 --> 00:25:37.203
<i>Ready for launch!</i>

513
00:25:37.495 --> 00:25:38.913
<i>PAW Patrol</i>

514
00:25:40.122 --> 00:25:41.749
Skye is go for launch.

515
00:25:41.957 --> 00:25:43.042
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Go!</i>

516
00:25:43.250 --> 00:25:44.710
(HORN SOUNDING)

517
00:25:46.462 --> 00:25:48.422
Whoa! That's got a kick to it!

518
00:25:51.592 --> 00:25:53.594
<i>PAW Patrol</i>

519
00:26:01.894 --> 00:26:03.020
(SIRENS BLARING)

520
00:26:04.397 --> 00:26:07.274
RYDER: PAW Patrol is on a roll...

521
00:26:07.358 --> 00:26:09.026
Are you kidding me?

522
00:26:09.110 --> 00:26:10.403
(CARS HONKING)

523
00:26:12.029 --> 00:26:14.198
Come on!
This is ridiculous!

524
00:26:14.448 --> 00:26:15.825
Green means go!

525
00:26:15.908 --> 00:26:17.743
Green means go!

526
00:26:18.494 --> 00:26:20.788
Green does still mean go, right?

527
00:26:21.622 --> 00:26:24.417
You're taking Main Street at rush hour?

528
00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:26.335
No wonder
you're stuck in traffic!

529
00:26:26.419 --> 00:26:28.754
(GRUNTS) I'm Liberty.
We spoke on the phone.

530
00:26:28.879 --> 00:26:31.132
So nice to finally meet you in person.

531
00:26:32.007 --> 00:26:33.342
Ryder.

532
00:26:33.426 --> 00:26:35.636
What your team needs is a pup like me.

533
00:26:35.886 --> 00:26:37.805
I know the city
like the back of my paw.

534
00:26:37.930 --> 00:26:40.599
Uptown, downtown, crosstown, midtown.

535
00:26:40.683 --> 00:26:43.936
24-7, 365, I'll get you
where you need to be!

536
00:26:44.019 --> 00:26:47.356
Well, we could use
a hand getting out of this traffic jam.

537
00:26:47.773 --> 00:26:50.401
That's what I'm talking about.
My first assignment!

538
00:26:50.776 --> 00:26:52.570
- Get out of the way! Move!
- Okay!

539
00:26:52.653 --> 00:26:53.779
- Move!
- (WHIMPERS)

540
00:26:54.780 --> 00:26:56.657
You've got to know
how to talk to people.

541
00:26:56.740 --> 00:26:57.741
Now go!

542
00:26:58.492 --> 00:26:59.702
RYDER: Excuse me.

543
00:26:59.785 --> 00:27:01.203
Pardon me! Coming through!

544
00:27:01.287 --> 00:27:02.538
Have a nice day!

545
00:27:02.621 --> 00:27:03.831
LIBERTY: Turn here!

546
00:27:06.792 --> 00:27:08.210
(SIRENS BLARING)

547
00:27:08.377 --> 00:27:09.503
Left!

548
00:27:09.587 --> 00:27:10.671
(TIRES SCREECHING)

549
00:27:11.297 --> 00:27:12.923
Right, then right again, right away!

550
00:27:13.215 --> 00:27:15.092
Whoa! Whoa!

551
00:27:16.010 --> 00:27:18.137
LIBERTY: Whoo-hoo!

552
00:27:18.637 --> 00:27:21.599
Ha-ha! You see that?
I'm like a furry GPS!

553
00:27:21.682 --> 00:27:22.725
Ahhh! Turn left!

554
00:27:23.017 --> 00:27:24.310
Whoa!

555
00:27:24.768 --> 00:27:26.145
(TIRES SCREECHING)

556
00:27:30.149 --> 00:27:32.318
You have reached your destination.

557
00:27:32.693 --> 00:27:34.069
(ALL SCREAMING)

558
00:27:34.695 --> 00:27:37.948
Now we know what happens when
you give Humdinger fireworks!

559
00:27:38.365 --> 00:27:40.034
The PAW Patrol?

560
00:27:40.117 --> 00:27:42.286
What are they doing
in Adventure City?

561
00:27:42.369 --> 00:27:44.121
Chase, set up a perimeter.

562
00:27:44.455 --> 00:27:46.165
Chase is on the case!

563
00:27:46.290 --> 00:27:47.583
(TIRES SCREECHING)

564
00:27:51.295 --> 00:27:52.379
(BEEPING)

565
00:27:56.509 --> 00:27:57.635
(CHEERING) PAW Patrol!

566
00:27:58.219 --> 00:27:59.220
Arf! Shields!

567
00:28:09.730 --> 00:28:12.274
Marshall, Rocky,
put out those fireworks!

568
00:28:12.358 --> 00:28:15.277
Let's kick the tires
and fight some fires!

569
00:28:16.278 --> 00:28:17.780
(HOWLING)

570
00:28:19.657 --> 00:28:22.117
Mr. Mayor, we've got
to get you out of here.

571
00:28:22.201 --> 00:28:24.828
I can't believe the PAW Patrol
crashed my party.

572
00:28:24.954 --> 00:28:27.122
- Yes, sir.
- I can't stand those dogs!

573
00:28:27.206 --> 00:28:28.457
Everyone knows
you're a cat person.

574
00:28:28.582 --> 00:28:29.959
- I can't stand them!
- Yes, sir.

575
00:28:30.042 --> 00:28:31.460
Hey, wait up!

576
00:28:31.544 --> 00:28:32.795
- (GRUNTS)
- (MEOWING)

577
00:28:36.715 --> 00:28:39.218
Time to fight some fireworks!

578
00:28:41.971 --> 00:28:43.806
We're gonna need more water!

579
00:28:44.098 --> 00:28:45.933
Arf! Water cannon!

580
00:28:51.564 --> 00:28:54.650
Yes! Now that's what I'm talking about.

581
00:28:55.317 --> 00:28:56.527
(WHIRRING)

582
00:29:03.325 --> 00:29:06.120
- Nice work, Marshall!
- Thank you.

583
00:29:06.745 --> 00:29:08.247
RYDER: Rocky, you're up!

584
00:29:08.330 --> 00:29:10.416
Okay, I got it from here!

585
00:29:12.585 --> 00:29:14.128
(FIREWORKS CRACKLING)

586
00:29:15.963 --> 00:29:17.256
(TIRES SCREECHING)

587
00:29:17.339 --> 00:29:18.966
And crush 'em!

588
00:29:20.259 --> 00:29:21.885
- (FIREWORKS EXPLODING)
- Whoa! Whoa!

589
00:29:22.177 --> 00:29:24.096
Whoa! Whoa!

590
00:29:24.179 --> 00:29:25.931
Ride 'em, cowboy!

591
00:29:26.599 --> 00:29:29.018
LIBERTY: (LAUGHING)
Look at him go!

592
00:29:29.977 --> 00:29:31.353
(SIRENS BLARING)

593
00:29:31.937 --> 00:29:33.230
(TIRES SCREECHING)

594
00:29:33.314 --> 00:29:34.732
CHASE: Perimeter secure!

595
00:29:36.734 --> 00:29:37.985
(PEOPLE SCREAMING IN DISTANCE)

596
00:29:38.068 --> 00:29:41.822
Ryder, we've got people
trapped on the balcony! I'm going in.

597
00:29:41.905 --> 00:29:42.906
RYDER: <i>Copy that.</i>

598
00:29:43.157 --> 00:29:45.200
- (SIRENS BLARING)
- (TIRES SCREECHING)

599
00:29:45.284 --> 00:29:46.619
Arf! Eject!

600
00:29:48.120 --> 00:29:49.955
Arf! Parachute!

601
00:29:53.751 --> 00:29:55.377
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

602
00:29:57.338 --> 00:29:58.881
Everything's going to be fine.

603
00:29:58.964 --> 00:30:00.466
I'm going to get you out of here.

604
00:30:01.550 --> 00:30:04.845
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

605
00:30:05.387 --> 00:30:06.597
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

606
00:30:06.680 --> 00:30:08.766
Ryder, help!

607
00:30:09.099 --> 00:30:11.143
Marshall! Chase needs help!

608
00:30:11.935 --> 00:30:13.520
I'm on it!

609
00:30:15.689 --> 00:30:16.774
(WHIRRING)

610
00:30:26.825 --> 00:30:28.077
(GASPING)

611
00:30:29.495 --> 00:30:30.954
(ALL CHEERING)

612
00:30:33.207 --> 00:30:35.668
Stand back!
Get away from the edge!

613
00:30:42.383 --> 00:30:43.884
Help me get him down!

614
00:30:44.885 --> 00:30:47.304
- Careful.
- MAN: Help me get him off.

615
00:30:47.388 --> 00:30:48.430
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

616
00:30:54.186 --> 00:30:56.230
It's okay, buddy. I've got you.

617
00:31:01.235 --> 00:31:02.611
(PEOPLE APPLAUDING)

618
00:31:02.945 --> 00:31:06.115
- WOMAN: Say cheese!
- ALL: Cheese!

619
00:31:06.198 --> 00:31:08.617
Hey! Hey! Anyone want
a picture with me?

620
00:31:08.701 --> 00:31:11.412
I'm kind of like an honorary
member of the PAW Patrol.

621
00:31:11.495 --> 00:31:12.705
You should have seen me out there.

622
00:31:12.830 --> 00:31:16.583
I was like, "Turn left, turn right,
turn left, turn right..."

623
00:31:16.709 --> 00:31:18.168
It was amazing!

624
00:31:22.631 --> 00:31:24.091
You look okay.

625
00:31:24.174 --> 00:31:25.634
How do you feel?

626
00:31:25.718 --> 00:31:28.345
I can't believe I forgot
to disconnect my parachute.

627
00:31:28.846 --> 00:31:30.889
It's Air Rescue 101.

628
00:31:31.432 --> 00:31:33.642
Well, that's why we're a team.

629
00:31:33.726 --> 00:31:37.271
Everyone pulled together,
and things worked out okay.

630
00:31:37.354 --> 00:31:38.814
But what if they didn't?

631
00:31:38.897 --> 00:31:41.817
What if something happened
to those people and it was all my fault?

632
00:31:45.571 --> 00:31:47.030
REPORTER: <i>Guardians. Heroes.</i>

633
00:31:47.114 --> 00:31:49.658
<i>Cute little dogs in adorable outfits.</i>

634
00:31:49.742 --> 00:31:52.161
<i>Whatever you call them,
the PAW Patrol were here</i>

635
00:31:52.286 --> 00:31:54.663
<i>to save the city
from Mayor Humdinger's</i>

636
00:31:54.747 --> 00:31:56.749
<i>- disastrous fireworks debacle.</i>
- (SCREAMING)

637
00:31:57.166 --> 00:32:00.961
<i>As a professional journalist,
it's important that I remain unbiased.</i>

638
00:32:01.044 --> 00:32:03.964
<i>That being said... Oh, yikes!</i>

639
00:32:04.173 --> 00:32:06.925
<i>An embarrassing start
for Mayor Humdinger,</i>

640
00:32:07.009 --> 00:32:11.555
<i>but an incredible debut
for the PAW Patrol in Adventure City!</i>

641
00:32:13.015 --> 00:32:15.392
PAW Patrol? PAW Patrol?

642
00:32:15.476 --> 00:32:18.520
I'm sick and tired
of hearing about the PAW Patrol!

643
00:32:18.604 --> 00:32:21.190
I came to Adventure City
to get away from them

644
00:32:21.273 --> 00:32:23.066
and make a name for myself.

645
00:32:23.150 --> 00:32:26.779
Now they're all over the TV
stealing my headlines!

646
00:32:26.862 --> 00:32:28.614
Butch! Ruben! Get in here!

647
00:32:28.739 --> 00:32:29.865
- (GROANS)
- Oh!

648
00:32:30.324 --> 00:32:31.408
Sorry, sir.

649
00:32:32.034 --> 00:32:35.037
I want the PAW Patrol
off the streets now!

650
00:32:35.120 --> 00:32:39.249
Find them, catch them,
and lock them away.

651
00:32:39.333 --> 00:32:40.709
- Yes, sir.
- Right away, sir.

652
00:32:42.586 --> 00:32:47.466
The PAW Patrol
have humiliated me for the last time!

653
00:32:47.925 --> 00:32:49.802
Sorry, did you say something?

654
00:32:49.885 --> 00:32:51.470
What? No, no!

655
00:32:51.553 --> 00:32:53.555
I was just having a private moment!

656
00:32:53.639 --> 00:32:55.057
Now get out of here!

657
00:32:59.978 --> 00:33:01.772
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

658
00:33:11.281 --> 00:33:12.407
(SNORING)

659
00:33:21.875 --> 00:33:25.921
<i>Just a jump away
from where you wanna go</i>

660
00:33:27.256 --> 00:33:31.260
<i>But you're too afraid
of doing it alone</i>

661
00:33:32.511 --> 00:33:36.139
<i>So getting halfway there
is all you've ever known</i>

662
00:33:36.223 --> 00:33:39.226
- (SIGHS)
<i>- I've been down that road</i>

663
00:33:41.937 --> 00:33:44.523
<i>Ooh</i>

664
00:33:53.240 --> 00:33:55.742
<i>Hold your head up</i>

665
00:33:55.951 --> 00:33:58.287
<i>You'll find your way home</i>

666
00:33:59.288 --> 00:34:02.082
<i>You won't get what you give sometimes</i>

667
00:34:03.375 --> 00:34:05.836
<i>-But when the dust all settles</i>
-(YAWNING)

668
00:34:06.461 --> 00:34:08.839
<i>And the smoke all clears up</i>

669
00:34:09.131 --> 00:34:12.175
<i>It's pieces of yourself
you're gonna find</i>

670
00:34:12.551 --> 00:34:15.429
<i>Maybe that's the use in trying</i>

671
00:34:19.892 --> 00:34:22.978
<i>It's pieces of yourself
you're gonna find</i>

672
00:34:23.061 --> 00:34:26.273
<i>Maybe that's the use in trying</i>

673
00:34:26.398 --> 00:34:27.774
(HUMMING)

674
00:34:27.858 --> 00:34:29.109
(METAL CREAKING)

675
00:34:29.484 --> 00:34:31.153
(LAUGHING) Liberty!

676
00:34:31.403 --> 00:34:33.447
I hear that sound, and I know it's you.

677
00:34:33.822 --> 00:34:35.616
"Eee-ooo-eee-ooo-eee-ooo!"

678
00:34:35.782 --> 00:34:39.036
I know, I know, I've got
to get my wagon fixed.

679
00:34:39.328 --> 00:34:41.830
So, how's the fruit business, Tony?

680
00:34:41.914 --> 00:34:45.125
Well, it would be better if I wasn't
always giving you free fruit.

681
00:34:45.250 --> 00:34:48.587
Hey, you hear about
that fireworks fiasco last night?

682
00:34:48.712 --> 00:34:51.465
I didn't just hear about it,
I was there.

683
00:34:51.548 --> 00:34:54.760
Honestly, Tony,
it was the best night of my life.

684
00:34:55.052 --> 00:34:59.014
For a few hours, it was like
I was a real member of the PAW Patrol.

685
00:34:59.097 --> 00:35:00.432
Imagine that, huh?

686
00:35:00.515 --> 00:35:04.519
"The newest member of
the PAW Patrol, Liberty!"

687
00:35:04.603 --> 00:35:06.313
Yeah, right, I wish.

688
00:35:06.521 --> 00:35:09.149
I heard that new mayor
is monkeying with the subway now.

689
00:35:09.232 --> 00:35:11.276
You better stay off
those trains, kiddo.

690
00:35:11.360 --> 00:35:14.196
- Stick to your wagon.
- Thanks for the tip, Tony.

691
00:35:14.738 --> 00:35:17.199
Hey, Liberty. Take one for the road!

692
00:35:17.282 --> 00:35:18.575
Thank you!

693
00:35:18.659 --> 00:35:19.743
(LAUGHING)

694
00:35:20.410 --> 00:35:24.915
(WHIRRING)

695
00:35:27.334 --> 00:35:28.502
(DINGING)

696
00:35:29.419 --> 00:35:30.504
(CLICKING)

697
00:35:31.046 --> 00:35:32.130
(SIGHS)

698
00:35:32.214 --> 00:35:34.841
Another perfect day in Adventure City.

699
00:35:34.925 --> 00:35:37.135
Enjoy that sunbeam, kitties.

700
00:35:37.219 --> 00:35:38.220
(PURRING)

701
00:35:38.553 --> 00:35:39.596
Mr. Mayor!

702
00:35:39.680 --> 00:35:42.766
The Cloud Catcher's
hygrometer is overloading the capacity

703
00:35:42.849 --> 00:35:45.394
of its pressurized internal
containment chamber!

704
00:35:45.811 --> 00:35:49.106
What? Do I look like a scientist to you?

705
00:35:49.481 --> 00:35:52.567
We need to bring down
the Cloud Catcher now!

706
00:35:52.651 --> 00:35:54.820
And ruin this beautiful weather?

707
00:35:54.903 --> 00:35:58.115
The Cloud Catcher
wasn't designed to run non-stop.

708
00:35:58.198 --> 00:36:00.242
Nonsense! As long as I'm mayor,

709
00:36:00.325 --> 00:36:03.286
the sun will always shine
on Adventure City.

710
00:36:03.370 --> 00:36:04.746
Now get her out of here.

711
00:36:05.247 --> 00:36:06.832
- BOTH: Get out of here!
- (GROANS)

712
00:36:06.915 --> 00:36:09.626
What are you doin'? I'm the one who
tells people to get out of here.

713
00:36:09.793 --> 00:36:11.336
No, you're not. I'm in charge!

714
00:36:11.420 --> 00:36:12.963
- No, I'm in charge!
- I'm in charge!

715
00:36:13.046 --> 00:36:14.631
- I'm in charge!
- (BOTH GROANING)

716
00:36:17.134 --> 00:36:18.552
Citizens of Adventure City!

717
00:36:18.885 --> 00:36:21.680
As your new, and already favorite,
mayor,

718
00:36:22.264 --> 00:36:24.933
I proudly present
the next step in my plan

719
00:36:25.017 --> 00:36:27.728
to put the adventure in Adventure City.

720
00:36:30.022 --> 00:36:32.315
The Humdinger Hyperloop!

721
00:36:32.399 --> 00:36:35.235
The kookiest, swoopiest,
loop-de-loopiest subway

722
00:36:35.318 --> 00:36:37.738
the world has ever seen!

723
00:36:38.780 --> 00:36:40.657
Mmm-mmm. I am not riding that thing.

724
00:36:40.991 --> 00:36:42.325
Mr. Mayor, Mr. Mayor!

725
00:36:42.409 --> 00:36:46.413
Have you considered the possibility
that this is the single dumbest idea

726
00:36:46.496 --> 00:36:49.624
that anyone has ever had ever?

727
00:36:50.125 --> 00:36:52.085
I'm an unqualified elected official.

728
00:36:52.169 --> 00:36:54.129
What's the worst that could happen?

729
00:36:54.796 --> 00:36:57.924
Look, here comes the express train now.

730
00:36:58.008 --> 00:36:59.843
Throw the switch, kitties!

731
00:36:59.926 --> 00:37:00.969
(MEOWING)

732
00:37:02.971 --> 00:37:04.139
(METAL CREAKING)

733
00:37:06.641 --> 00:37:07.976
(CREAKING)

734
00:37:08.060 --> 00:37:09.352
(ALL SCREAMING)

735
00:37:10.687 --> 00:37:13.440
Whee! (LAUGHING)

736
00:37:14.441 --> 00:37:16.318
(PASSENGERS SCREAMING)

737
00:37:17.027 --> 00:37:18.070
(CLANKING)

738
00:37:20.864 --> 00:37:22.240
(SCREECHING)

739
00:37:30.373 --> 00:37:32.084
(ALL SCREAMING)

740
00:37:32.334 --> 00:37:34.753
Ooh! That is not good.

741
00:37:35.295 --> 00:37:37.339
Butch, get the car.
Ruben, get the kitties.

742
00:37:37.422 --> 00:37:39.049
Time for me to vamoose!

743
00:37:41.259 --> 00:37:42.803
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

744
00:37:44.137 --> 00:37:45.305
(PHONE RINGING)

745
00:37:46.681 --> 00:37:48.433
RYDER: PAW Patrol,
what's your emergency?

746
00:37:48.517 --> 00:37:50.602
<i>Help! Help us!</i>

747
00:37:50.727 --> 00:37:53.855
<i>Mayor Humdingerstuck a loop-de-loop in
the middle of the subway track,</i>

748
00:37:53.939 --> 00:37:55.816
<i>and now, we're hanging on
for dear life!</i>

749
00:37:56.942 --> 00:38:00.153
<i>This is a new low for subway service
in this city,</i>

750
00:38:00.237 --> 00:38:02.239
<i>and that is saying something!</i>

751
00:38:02.322 --> 00:38:04.324
Hang tight! We're on our way!

752
00:38:04.658 --> 00:38:05.700
Okay, pups.

753
00:38:05.826 --> 00:38:08.036
We've got to rescue
the passengers on that train

754
00:38:08.120 --> 00:38:10.288
before the whole thing
comes crashing down.

755
00:38:10.372 --> 00:38:11.665
Let's move!

756
00:38:11.748 --> 00:38:14.000
PAW Patrol is on a roll!

757
00:38:14.126 --> 00:38:15.418
ALL: Yeah!

758
00:38:17.587 --> 00:38:21.633
Marty Muckraker reporting live
from Mayor Humdinger's latest disaster.

759
00:38:21.716 --> 00:38:25.470
In a surprising twist
that surprised nobody,

760
00:38:25.554 --> 00:38:27.556
the shoddily built upside-down subway

761
00:38:27.639 --> 00:38:30.308
turned out to be a steaming hot pile of,

762
00:38:30.392 --> 00:38:32.894
<i>dare I say, poop.</i>

763
00:38:33.103 --> 00:38:34.312
(TRUCK HONKING)

764
00:38:34.396 --> 00:38:36.523
GIRL: <i>Look, Mom, the PAW Patrol!</i>

765
00:38:36.606 --> 00:38:37.983
(SIRENS BLARING)

766
00:38:39.317 --> 00:38:42.904
I can't believe Humdinger
thought this was a good idea.

767
00:38:43.071 --> 00:38:45.782
The subway's wild enough
without a stinkin' loop-de-loop!

768
00:38:46.324 --> 00:38:48.034
Hey, Liberty!

769
00:38:48.118 --> 00:38:49.536
Reporting for duty.

770
00:38:50.370 --> 00:38:53.415
Unofficially, of course.
You know, like an honorary member.

771
00:38:53.498 --> 00:38:55.333
- (METAL CREAKING)
- (GASPS)

772
00:38:57.002 --> 00:38:59.254
Rocky, I need you
to stabilize that loop.

773
00:38:59.337 --> 00:39:01.381
Rubble, see if you can
lock it into place

774
00:39:01.464 --> 00:39:02.632
with some quick-dry cement.

775
00:39:02.883 --> 00:39:04.050
BOTH: We're on it!

776
00:39:04.259 --> 00:39:07.095
RYDER: Skye, I need you
to secure that loop from the air.

777
00:39:07.262 --> 00:39:09.306
Let's take to the sky!

778
00:39:10.098 --> 00:39:11.683
(CROWD CHEERING)

779
00:39:12.392 --> 00:39:15.896
Don't worry, Ryder, I've got
crowd control under control.

780
00:39:16.188 --> 00:39:18.356
Stand back! Give us some space!

781
00:39:18.440 --> 00:39:19.733
PAW Patrol at work!

782
00:39:19.858 --> 00:39:21.651
I'm an honorary member
at the moment,

783
00:39:21.776 --> 00:39:23.987
but my authority
should still be respected.

784
00:39:24.196 --> 00:39:25.405
(CREAKING)

785
00:39:31.912 --> 00:39:33.955
Arf! Hydraulic arms!

786
00:39:35.874 --> 00:39:37.292
(TIRES SCREECHING)

787
00:39:37.542 --> 00:39:38.793
Gotcha!

788
00:39:44.549 --> 00:39:46.218
- Hey, look!
- It's Skye!

789
00:39:50.222 --> 00:39:52.349
Time for a little more power.

790
00:39:52.641 --> 00:39:54.809
Arf! Afterburners!

791
00:40:02.484 --> 00:40:04.819
Okay, Rubble, let 'er rip!

792
00:40:05.111 --> 00:40:06.363
(HOWLING)

793
00:40:06.821 --> 00:40:08.907
Rubble on the double!

794
00:40:19.376 --> 00:40:20.710
RUBBLE: The track is secure!

795
00:40:21.127 --> 00:40:22.337
SKYE: Yeah, Rubble!

796
00:40:23.171 --> 00:40:24.547
Nice work, Rubble!

797
00:40:25.006 --> 00:40:27.092
Chase, we've got to rescue those people.

798
00:40:27.384 --> 00:40:28.677
Are you up for it?

799
00:40:29.511 --> 00:40:31.179
Chase is on the case.

800
00:40:31.263 --> 00:40:32.430
(GRUNTS)

801
00:40:32.555 --> 00:40:34.391
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

802
00:40:42.148 --> 00:40:43.233
(GRUNTS)

803
00:40:49.614 --> 00:40:51.449
(PASSENGERS PANICKING)

804
00:40:51.574 --> 00:40:53.785
Hang on! You're going to be okay.

805
00:40:54.452 --> 00:40:55.912
Arf! Zipline!

806
00:40:58.873 --> 00:41:00.375
(PASSENGERS CHEERING)

807
00:41:01.584 --> 00:41:04.129
PASSENGERS: (CHEERING)
Chase! Chase! Chase!

808
00:41:04.462 --> 00:41:06.047
RYDER: <i>How are you holding up, Chase?</i>

809
00:41:06.131 --> 00:41:07.132
I'm fine.

810
00:41:07.215 --> 00:41:08.216
<i>Are you sure?</i>

811
00:41:08.300 --> 00:41:09.301
I can do this!

812
00:41:09.384 --> 00:41:10.927
- PASSENGERS: Chase! Chase!
- You can do it, Chase!

813
00:41:11.011 --> 00:41:12.178
I can do this.

814
00:41:12.262 --> 00:41:14.306
PASSENGERS: Chase! Chase!

815
00:41:14.764 --> 00:41:16.016
CHASE: I can do this.

816
00:41:18.101 --> 00:41:19.269
I can...

817
00:41:19.352 --> 00:41:20.645
(GASPS)

818
00:41:20.812 --> 00:41:22.022
(WHIMPERING)

819
00:41:23.565 --> 00:41:25.275
(BREATHING RAPIDLY)

820
00:41:26.318 --> 00:41:28.361
RYDER: <i>Chase? Chase, do you copy?</i>

821
00:41:29.612 --> 00:41:31.072
(HELICOPTER WHIRRING)

822
00:41:32.240 --> 00:41:34.200
Ryder, we've got a problem.

823
00:41:34.576 --> 00:41:35.577
What's going on?

824
00:41:35.660 --> 00:41:37.620
It's Chase. Something's wrong.

825
00:41:37.704 --> 00:41:39.247
He's just standing there.

826
00:41:44.210 --> 00:41:47.130
Chase is in trouble.
Skye, bring him down.

827
00:41:47.380 --> 00:41:49.466
Marshall, get your ladder up
to the train.

828
00:41:49.591 --> 00:41:50.759
I'm on it!

829
00:41:51.343 --> 00:41:52.927
(SIREN BLARING)

830
00:41:55.805 --> 00:41:57.140
(CREAKING)

831
00:41:58.224 --> 00:41:59.726
(SIREN BLARING)

832
00:42:01.936 --> 00:42:03.855
I think I can reach them from here.

833
00:42:04.147 --> 00:42:05.398
Arf! Ladder!

834
00:42:09.152 --> 00:42:10.362
(WHIRRING)

835
00:42:24.918 --> 00:42:27.796
MARSHALL ON SPEAKER: <i>Please exit
the train and proceed down the ladder.</i>

836
00:42:28.296 --> 00:42:29.547
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

837
00:42:31.132 --> 00:42:32.675
This should speed things up.

838
00:42:33.134 --> 00:42:34.928
Arf! Ladder slide!

839
00:42:36.721 --> 00:42:38.515
Here goes nothing!

840
00:42:39.057 --> 00:42:40.517
Whoo-hoo!

841
00:42:42.852 --> 00:42:44.521
RYDER: <i>Nice work, Marshall!</i>

842
00:42:51.403 --> 00:42:52.404
Chase?

843
00:42:52.737 --> 00:42:54.614
I'm coming out to get you.

844
00:42:56.991 --> 00:42:58.410
What's wrong?

845
00:42:58.493 --> 00:42:59.744
Tell me what happened.

846
00:43:00.328 --> 00:43:01.579
I don't know.

847
00:43:01.955 --> 00:43:05.083
I just... froze.

848
00:43:06.042 --> 00:43:09.754
It's okay. Everyone's safe.
Let's get you down.

849
00:43:21.141 --> 00:43:22.350
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

850
00:43:38.158 --> 00:43:40.285
Okay, that's all of them.

851
00:43:40.368 --> 00:43:41.953
Good job, pups.

852
00:43:43.955 --> 00:43:45.165
Chase...

853
00:43:46.541 --> 00:43:48.209
I don't know what happened.

854
00:43:48.835 --> 00:43:50.336
I'm just glad you're okay.

855
00:43:51.671 --> 00:43:54.966
- I'm sorry.
- No, it's my fault.

856
00:43:55.425 --> 00:43:57.594
I thought you'd be okay
in Adventure City,

857
00:43:57.677 --> 00:43:59.471
but it's still too much for you.

858
00:43:59.554 --> 00:44:01.306
I'll be fine. I just need to...

859
00:44:01.389 --> 00:44:04.392
You're not fine.
You need to take a break.

860
00:44:04.601 --> 00:44:06.978
We'll take care of the rescues
for a while.

861
00:44:07.353 --> 00:44:09.105
What? No!

862
00:44:09.230 --> 00:44:10.899
That's not fair.

863
00:44:11.316 --> 00:44:12.901
I'm sorry, Chase.

864
00:44:13.026 --> 00:44:15.987
I know it's hard,
but it's the way it's got to be.

865
00:44:18.406 --> 00:44:20.783
I didn't even want to come
to Adventure City!

866
00:44:20.867 --> 00:44:22.160
I trusted you.

867
00:44:22.243 --> 00:44:25.246
You said everything
would be fine, but it's not!

868
00:44:25.455 --> 00:44:29.000
What kind of leader gives up
on someone the second things get hard?

869
00:44:29.083 --> 00:44:30.293
Chase...

870
00:44:32.462 --> 00:44:33.838
Chase, wait!

871
00:44:34.005 --> 00:44:35.715
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

872
00:44:39.761 --> 00:44:41.054
(PANTING)

873
00:44:54.651 --> 00:44:55.735
RUBEN: Oh-ho!

874
00:44:55.818 --> 00:44:56.945
What do we have here?

875
00:44:57.153 --> 00:45:00.865
Looks like we got
one of them PAW Patrols all on his own.

876
00:45:00.949 --> 00:45:03.117
- Get the net.
- (LAUGHING)

877
00:45:04.327 --> 00:45:06.663
RYDER: Chase? Chase!

878
00:45:07.163 --> 00:45:09.123
- Come on, Chase.
- Chase?

879
00:45:09.207 --> 00:45:10.583
Chase!

880
00:45:10.667 --> 00:45:12.377
Hey, buddy, where are you?

881
00:45:12.502 --> 00:45:15.505
Where'd you go, bud? Chase!

882
00:45:21.469 --> 00:45:23.888
- Oh, no.
- Where did he go?

883
00:45:24.931 --> 00:45:26.474
I was right behind him.

884
00:45:26.599 --> 00:45:28.685
I turned the corner
and he was gone.

885
00:45:29.435 --> 00:45:31.229
He just disappeared.

886
00:45:31.896 --> 00:45:34.232
- What are we going to do?
- I don't know.

887
00:45:34.315 --> 00:45:37.443
There's no way for us to track him
if he's not wearing his pup tag.

888
00:45:38.319 --> 00:45:40.071
We might not have a tracking collar,

889
00:45:40.196 --> 00:45:42.991
but the city has eyes,
and the city has ears.

890
00:45:43.157 --> 00:45:44.826
Somebody had to see something.

891
00:45:44.909 --> 00:45:47.120
Okay. Where do we start?

892
00:45:47.203 --> 00:45:48.788
We need to pound the pavement.

893
00:45:48.871 --> 00:45:50.915
- I'll get my jackhammer!
- (PUPS LAUGHING)

894
00:45:50.999 --> 00:45:52.917
No, not like that.

895
00:45:53.001 --> 00:45:55.795
"Pound the pavement" means we're gonna
need to talk to everyone.

896
00:45:55.878 --> 00:45:57.005
Ask questions.

897
00:45:57.171 --> 00:45:58.715
Leave no stone unturned.

898
00:45:58.840 --> 00:46:01.551
Then I'll get the stone
turning attachment for my dozer.

899
00:46:01.718 --> 00:46:02.760
(PUPS LAUGHING)

900
00:46:02.927 --> 00:46:04.512
Can someone please explain it to him?

901
00:46:04.596 --> 00:46:05.680
(HONKING)

902
00:46:05.763 --> 00:46:08.308
Out of the way! Learn to drive!

903
00:46:08.391 --> 00:46:10.310
Someone should take away his license.

904
00:46:11.060 --> 00:46:12.145
(GRUNTS)

905
00:46:12.562 --> 00:46:14.188
Stop this vehicle right now!

906
00:46:14.606 --> 00:46:16.691
I'm a police dog
and you're under arrest!

907
00:46:16.983 --> 00:46:19.068
Oh, no! You hear that, Butch?

908
00:46:19.193 --> 00:46:20.862
We're under arrest.

909
00:46:20.945 --> 00:46:22.322
(BOTH LAUGHING)

910
00:46:22.614 --> 00:46:24.782
Hey, why do you get to wear the hat?

911
00:46:24.866 --> 00:46:26.242
'Cause I took it from him!

912
00:46:26.326 --> 00:46:27.744
Well, I'm taking it from you!

913
00:46:27.869 --> 00:46:30.538
- Give me that back, it's my hat! My hat!
- No, it's my hat!

914
00:46:30.622 --> 00:46:31.706
(BOTH GROANING)

915
00:46:31.789 --> 00:46:33.291
Hey, hands on the wheel!

916
00:46:33.374 --> 00:46:34.792
Ahhh!

917
00:46:35.585 --> 00:46:37.503
So unprofessional!

918
00:46:42.550 --> 00:46:43.593
(CLANKING)

919
00:46:44.677 --> 00:46:45.803
(DOGS BARKING)

920
00:46:45.928 --> 00:46:47.055
(CHASE GRUNTING)

921
00:46:47.764 --> 00:46:49.307
Quit squirming!

922
00:46:49.390 --> 00:46:50.558
(GRUNTING)

923
00:46:51.142 --> 00:46:52.185
(SQUEALING)

924
00:46:52.268 --> 00:46:54.937
Put me down! Let me go!

925
00:46:55.063 --> 00:46:56.397
- (CHASE GRUNTS)
- (DOOR BUZZING)

926
00:46:57.899 --> 00:47:00.068
Welcome to your new home.

927
00:47:00.151 --> 00:47:01.569
(LAUGHS)

928
00:47:03.738 --> 00:47:06.074
(BANGING)

929
00:47:08.034 --> 00:47:09.452
What is this place?

930
00:47:09.744 --> 00:47:12.121
It's Fuzzy Buddies Obedience School!

931
00:47:12.205 --> 00:47:14.791
- Isn't it awesome?
- What?

932
00:47:14.916 --> 00:47:16.709
We're gonna learn so many new tricks,

933
00:47:16.793 --> 00:47:20.880
like sit, and roll over, and, uh, sit.

934
00:47:21.839 --> 00:47:25.134
Ugh, Barney, how many times
do I have to tell you?

935
00:47:25.218 --> 00:47:27.387
It's not an obedience school anymore.

936
00:47:27.595 --> 00:47:29.931
Mayor Humdinger's goons
took over this place

937
00:47:30.014 --> 00:47:31.933
and turned it into a jail.

938
00:47:32.016 --> 00:47:34.977
Old Humdinger's
not exactly a dog lover.

939
00:47:35.061 --> 00:47:36.938
He's more of a cat person.

940
00:47:37.230 --> 00:47:38.439
(MOANING IN DISGUST)

941
00:47:38.523 --> 00:47:40.400
He's rounding up
all the dogs in the city,

942
00:47:40.525 --> 00:47:42.402
and locking us in here.

943
00:47:42.485 --> 00:47:43.986
That's terrible.

944
00:47:44.070 --> 00:47:45.822
Never let your guard down in here.

945
00:47:45.905 --> 00:47:48.324
There's one guy you gotta watch out for.

946
00:47:48.408 --> 00:47:52.036
He'll sneak up behind you
when you least expect it.

947
00:47:52.745 --> 00:47:53.996
There he is!

948
00:47:54.080 --> 00:47:56.249
Don't worry, guys, I'll protect you!

949
00:47:56.374 --> 00:47:58.793
Leave my friends alone! Ow!

950
00:47:59.001 --> 00:48:00.169
(BARKING)

951
00:48:00.712 --> 00:48:02.588
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

952
00:48:03.756 --> 00:48:05.383
He got away!

953
00:48:06.008 --> 00:48:08.010
I gotta get out of here.

954
00:48:08.261 --> 00:48:09.846
So what's your story, kid?

955
00:48:10.847 --> 00:48:12.515
I don't even know anymore.

956
00:48:13.099 --> 00:48:15.393
I thought I was a member
of the PAW Patrol.

957
00:48:15.476 --> 00:48:17.895
But now I feel like
they're better off without me.

958
00:48:17.979 --> 00:48:20.189
What makes you say a thing like that?

959
00:48:20.273 --> 00:48:22.859
I keep messing up
and letting everyone down.

960
00:48:24.068 --> 00:48:27.864
(SIGHING) I can't even,
with all this negativity.

961
00:48:28.197 --> 00:48:30.742
Just ignore her.
She's all bark and no bite.

962
00:48:30.950 --> 00:48:32.660
Now pick yourself a doghouse.

963
00:48:32.785 --> 00:48:34.454
You're gonna be here awhile.

964
00:48:36.789 --> 00:48:38.374
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

965
00:48:40.293 --> 00:48:41.836
(DOGS BARKING IN DISTANCE)

966
00:48:48.134 --> 00:48:49.802
Come on, in here!

967
00:48:49.886 --> 00:48:50.970
(BELL TINKLING)

968
00:48:51.053 --> 00:48:52.180
Liberty!

969
00:48:52.305 --> 00:48:53.598
<i>Que gusto verte!</i>

970
00:48:53.723 --> 00:48:55.433
How's life treating you these days?

971
00:48:55.516 --> 00:48:57.393
Carmen, I got no time for chitchat.

972
00:48:57.518 --> 00:48:59.604
We're in a jam and we need your help.

973
00:48:59.687 --> 00:49:01.063
Have you seen this dog?

974
00:49:01.522 --> 00:49:04.317
No, I haven't seen him.

975
00:49:04.400 --> 00:49:07.320
If you want, you can put
his picture up on the wall.

976
00:49:09.322 --> 00:49:10.448
Whoa...

977
00:49:11.991 --> 00:49:14.619
Lots of dogs going missing lately.

978
00:49:15.161 --> 00:49:16.996
I'm keeping my eyes open

979
00:49:17.079 --> 00:49:20.750
but it's like they just disappear.

980
00:49:20.875 --> 00:49:22.585
How long has this been happening?

981
00:49:22.668 --> 00:49:24.712
It started a couple days ago.

982
00:49:24.796 --> 00:49:27.632
Now, half my customers
are missing a dog.

983
00:49:27.757 --> 00:49:29.300
This can't be a coincidence.

984
00:49:29.383 --> 00:49:31.219
Somebody's got to be taking them.

985
00:49:31.302 --> 00:49:33.679
Dog-napping? Who would do that?

986
00:49:33.763 --> 00:49:35.973
Humdinger! It's got to be him.

987
00:49:36.057 --> 00:49:38.017
He hates dogs more than anything.

988
00:49:38.100 --> 00:49:39.644
But where is he taking them?

989
00:49:39.727 --> 00:49:41.562
I think I know how we can find out.

990
00:49:41.813 --> 00:49:43.397
- How?
- I'm a dog.

991
00:49:43.523 --> 00:49:45.817
I'm also kind of an honorary
member of the PAW Patrol,

992
00:49:45.942 --> 00:49:47.318
so I'll be the bait.

993
00:49:47.443 --> 00:49:49.403
I get captured, you tail me,

994
00:49:49.529 --> 00:49:51.948
and boom, we find out
where he's taking them.

995
00:49:52.031 --> 00:49:54.075
That might actually work.

996
00:49:54.200 --> 00:49:56.744
We just need to figure out how
to get Humdinger's attention.

997
00:49:57.537 --> 00:49:58.871
Leave that to me.

998
00:50:02.792 --> 00:50:05.711
<i>Marty Muckraker here,
bringing you an exclusive interview</i>

999
00:50:05.837 --> 00:50:08.256
<i>with recently disgraced
Mayor Humdinger.</i>

1000
00:50:08.339 --> 00:50:09.423
<i>Thanks, Marty.</i>

1001
00:50:09.507 --> 00:50:12.301
<i>After today's little subway snafu,</i>

1002
00:50:12.385 --> 00:50:14.303
<i>I just wanted to assure the public</i>

1003
00:50:14.428 --> 00:50:16.889
<i>there will be no more
embarrassing mishaps.</i>

1004
00:50:16.973 --> 00:50:18.391
- (LIBERTY SCREAMS)
<i>- Ahhh!</i>

1005
00:50:18.599 --> 00:50:20.226
<i>Put a cork in it, windbag!</i>

1006
00:50:20.309 --> 00:50:21.978
Somebody get this filthy dog away
from me!

1007
00:50:22.061 --> 00:50:23.688
(LIBERTY LAUGHS)

1008
00:50:24.647 --> 00:50:25.773
Gotcha!

1009
00:50:26.274 --> 00:50:27.525
(LAUGHING)

1010
00:50:28.609 --> 00:50:31.696
(GASPS) Oh, no! Please! Let me go!

1011
00:50:31.863 --> 00:50:34.824
Don't take me to exactly
the same place you took the other dogs,

1012
00:50:34.907 --> 00:50:39.620
in this white van,
license plate number YVP 8624!

1013
00:50:41.330 --> 00:50:42.915
You, with the pants on your head,

1014
00:50:42.999 --> 00:50:45.167
- get me a new pair of pants.
- Right away, sir!

1015
00:50:45.251 --> 00:50:46.919
When my new pants arrive,

1016
00:50:47.003 --> 00:50:49.213
we'll take this interview from the top.

1017
00:50:49.297 --> 00:50:51.841
Um... Mr. Mayor, we're live.

1018
00:50:52.800 --> 00:50:53.885
(LAUGHING)

1019
00:50:54.468 --> 00:50:56.053
<i>- Ahhh!</i>
- (PEOPLE LAUGHING)

1020
00:50:56.846 --> 00:50:59.682
<i>If this goes viral,
I'm canceling the Internet!</i>

1021
00:51:07.773 --> 00:51:08.858
(BARKING)

1022
00:51:08.941 --> 00:51:10.610
Get back here! I'm gonna get you!

1023
00:51:10.860 --> 00:51:11.986
(CLATTERING)

1024
00:51:17.074 --> 00:51:18.242
(DOOR BUZZING)

1025
00:51:18.409 --> 00:51:22.121
Was this one easier to catch,
or are we getting better at this?

1026
00:51:22.288 --> 00:51:25.291
Oh-ho-ho!
We're definitely getting better at this.

1027
00:51:25.374 --> 00:51:27.001
- (CHUCKLING)
- (DOOR LOCKING)

1028
00:51:27.084 --> 00:51:28.586
Chase? Chase?

1029
00:51:28.920 --> 00:51:32.798
Anybody here seen a German Shepherd
about yay high, always saying,

1030
00:51:32.924 --> 00:51:34.258
"Chase is on the case"?

1031
00:51:34.800 --> 00:51:35.801
Liberty?

1032
00:51:36.344 --> 00:51:37.553
Hey, buddy!

1033
00:51:37.887 --> 00:51:39.430
I came to bust you out of here.

1034
00:51:39.513 --> 00:51:40.973
Puh-lease.

1035
00:51:41.057 --> 00:51:44.518
This scrawny little purse pup
is going to pull a jailbreak?

1036
00:51:44.894 --> 00:51:47.855
You talk a lot of trash
for a dog who looks like a toilet brush.

1037
00:51:48.522 --> 00:51:49.607
Hmph!

1038
00:51:49.690 --> 00:51:51.233
Come on, Chase, get up.

1039
00:51:51.776 --> 00:51:53.569
You shouldn't have come after me.

1040
00:51:53.653 --> 00:51:55.029
Now we're both stuck in here.

1041
00:51:55.571 --> 00:51:57.365
Of course I came after you.

1042
00:51:57.782 --> 00:52:01.619
I might just be one small pup,
all alone in the big city,

1043
00:52:01.702 --> 00:52:03.412
but I can still make a difference.

1044
00:52:03.871 --> 00:52:06.874
I can still be a hero, just like you.

1045
00:52:09.210 --> 00:52:11.295
- I'm no hero.
- Yeah, right.

1046
00:52:11.379 --> 00:52:13.756
And I'm a purebred show dog with papers.

1047
00:52:15.341 --> 00:52:17.468
Oh... You're serious.

1048
00:52:17.885 --> 00:52:22.473
I used to think I was a hero,
but it turns out I'm just scared.

1049
00:52:22.890 --> 00:52:25.267
So? Who cares if you're scared?

1050
00:52:25.851 --> 00:52:27.561
Heroes get scared all the time.

1051
00:52:28.187 --> 00:52:30.314
- They do?
- Of course they do.

1052
00:52:30.731 --> 00:52:33.985
But even though they're scared,
they push through and keep going.

1053
00:52:34.402 --> 00:52:36.195
That's what makes them heroes.

1054
00:52:38.990 --> 00:52:41.158
While you chew over
that knowledge I just dropped,

1055
00:52:41.242 --> 00:52:42.660
I'm gonna get us outta here.

1056
00:52:43.244 --> 00:52:44.787
We're stuck in here, Liberty.

1057
00:52:44.912 --> 00:52:47.623
That door is always locked,
and it's the only way out.

1058
00:52:48.332 --> 00:52:51.585
Well, there's one thing
I forgot to mention.

1059
00:52:52.003 --> 00:52:53.421
(RUMBLING)

1060
00:52:53.796 --> 00:52:55.339
I brought backup!

1061
00:52:55.756 --> 00:52:57.967
- Rubble!
- On the double!

1062
00:52:58.050 --> 00:52:59.635
<i>Three, two, one, go</i>

1063
00:52:59.719 --> 00:53:00.886
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

1064
00:53:00.970 --> 00:53:02.888
ALL: Yeah!

1065
00:53:04.306 --> 00:53:05.599
Chase!

1066
00:53:05.725 --> 00:53:06.851
(DOOR BUZZING)

1067
00:53:06.934 --> 00:53:08.936
- What's going on in here?
- What's going on in here?

1068
00:53:09.895 --> 00:53:10.938
Get 'em!

1069
00:53:11.022 --> 00:53:12.732
- Charge!
- (BARKING)

1070
00:53:12.815 --> 00:53:14.150
(BOTH SCREAMING)

1071
00:53:16.902 --> 00:53:18.571
I'm gonna get ya!
I'm gonna get ya!

1072
00:53:18.654 --> 00:53:19.780
(DOORS BUZZING)

1073
00:53:19.864 --> 00:53:21.323
DOG: Yes, we're free!

1074
00:53:21.824 --> 00:53:23.409
- All right, pups, let's roll.
- (HOWLING)

1075
00:53:23.868 --> 00:53:25.745
Chase, you ride with me.

1076
00:53:25.911 --> 00:53:27.538
(RHYTHMIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1077
00:53:29.749 --> 00:53:31.709
- LIBERTY: Whoa!
- You cool back there, Liberty?

1078
00:53:32.043 --> 00:53:34.003
LIBERTY: I'm doing great! Ahhh!

1079
00:53:34.086 --> 00:53:35.921
(WHIMPERING)

1080
00:53:36.005 --> 00:53:39.175
Come on, you bucket of bolts,
don't quit on me now!

1081
00:53:40.134 --> 00:53:41.594
Chase and I have to make a stop.

1082
00:53:41.677 --> 00:53:43.137
We'll meet you back at headquarters.

1083
00:53:43.220 --> 00:53:45.473
MARSHALL: Aye aye, Ryder, sir!
See you there.

1084
00:53:46.098 --> 00:53:47.266
(METALLIC CREAKING)

1085
00:53:51.771 --> 00:53:53.230
CHASE: Where are we going?

1086
00:53:53.647 --> 00:53:55.066
RYDER: There's something
I need to show you.

1087
00:53:56.567 --> 00:53:58.194
Do you remember this place?

1088
00:54:00.654 --> 00:54:02.281
This is where I found you.

1089
00:54:02.865 --> 00:54:04.909
Why would you bring me here?

1090
00:54:05.534 --> 00:54:08.370
I know this place reminds you of
the worst time in your life.

1091
00:54:08.913 --> 00:54:10.539
But there's more to it than that.

1092
00:54:11.165 --> 00:54:13.084
It's also a great place.

1093
00:54:13.250 --> 00:54:15.002
I remember the first time I saw you.

1094
00:54:16.712 --> 00:54:19.924
You were a tiny little pup,
all alone in the big city.

1095
00:54:22.843 --> 00:54:24.053
(GRUNTS)

1096
00:54:24.428 --> 00:54:25.638
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1097
00:54:26.180 --> 00:54:28.307
- (GASPS)
- (CAR HONKING)

1098
00:54:34.855 --> 00:54:37.691
I know. You saw me
and took pity on me.

1099
00:54:38.150 --> 00:54:39.193
Not at all.

1100
00:54:39.652 --> 00:54:41.904
<i>What I saw was a brave, heroic pup.</i>

1101
00:54:42.696 --> 00:54:45.157
<i>Even though you were too small
to look after yourself,</i>

1102
00:54:45.282 --> 00:54:47.409
<i>and you were up against
all those scary things,</i>

1103
00:54:47.493 --> 00:54:49.745
<i>you got back up and kept going.</i>

1104
00:54:50.037 --> 00:54:52.623
<i>I didn't adopt you
because I felt sorry for you.</i>

1105
00:54:53.040 --> 00:54:56.544
<i>I chose you because you were
the bravest pup I'd ever seen.</i>

1106
00:54:59.672 --> 00:55:01.340
I know Adventure City
has been tough for you,

1107
00:55:01.966 --> 00:55:05.970
but I also know that
deep down you were born to be a hero.

1108
00:55:08.389 --> 00:55:11.016
So, what do you say?
Wanna go to work?

1109
00:55:11.767 --> 00:55:13.936
Ready for action, Ryder sir.

1110
00:55:15.729 --> 00:55:17.231
(WHIRRING)

1111
00:55:19.608 --> 00:55:21.694
(BEEPING AND CLANKING)

1112
00:55:23.237 --> 00:55:25.406
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1113
00:55:26.031 --> 00:55:27.575
(RAP MUSIC PLAYING)

1114
00:55:31.162 --> 00:55:32.621
(MEOWING)

1115
00:55:33.998 --> 00:55:35.207
(GRUNTS)

1116
00:55:35.291 --> 00:55:36.584
Here you go, boss.

1117
00:55:37.126 --> 00:55:38.961
Let's make history.

1118
00:55:40.337 --> 00:55:41.881
- Mayor Humdinger!
- Ahhh!

1119
00:55:41.964 --> 00:55:44.258
Don't sneak up on me like that.

1120
00:55:44.341 --> 00:55:46.760
The Cloud Catcher's
precipometer has short-circuited

1121
00:55:46.844 --> 00:55:50.806
and the barometric pressure
has dropped below 87 kilopascals!

1122
00:55:50.890 --> 00:55:53.058
What? I never know
what you're talking about.

1123
00:55:53.142 --> 00:55:54.268
Dumb it down for me!

1124
00:55:54.435 --> 00:55:57.771
We've got to bring down
the Cloud Catcher, it's gonna blow!

1125
00:55:57.855 --> 00:55:59.565
Hogwash! Give me that.

1126
00:56:01.233 --> 00:56:02.902
(GASPS) What are you doing?

1127
00:56:03.068 --> 00:56:04.069
Hmm!

1128
00:56:05.821 --> 00:56:07.948
<i>There's a free-floating meteorological</i>

1129
00:56:08.032 --> 00:56:09.575
<i>weather containment system overhead,</i>

1130
00:56:09.700 --> 00:56:12.453
<i>and the anemometer readings
are off the charts!</i>

1131
00:56:12.953 --> 00:56:14.205
ALL: What?

1132
00:56:14.705 --> 00:56:17.666
<i>We're all in grave danger.</i>

1133
00:56:17.750 --> 00:56:20.085
<i>In danger of having the time
of our lives!</i>

1134
00:56:20.252 --> 00:56:22.796
<i>Thank you, Kendra,
for that lovely introduction.</i>

1135
00:56:23.214 --> 00:56:25.966
You're making a big mistake!

1136
00:56:26.759 --> 00:56:29.637
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
members of the press,</i>

1137
00:56:29.720 --> 00:56:31.347
<i>and most importantly</i>

1138
00:56:31.764 --> 00:56:33.724
<i>influencers with over
10,000 followers,</i>

1139
00:56:34.141 --> 00:56:35.643
<i>we are gathered here today</i>

1140
00:56:35.768 --> 00:56:39.355
<i>for the grand opening
of Humdinger Heights!</i>

1141
00:56:40.564 --> 00:56:41.941
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1142
00:56:42.942 --> 00:56:46.195
<i>I took the tallest skyscraper
in Adventure City</i>

1143
00:56:46.278 --> 00:56:49.198
<i>and stuck a brand-new tower on top,</i>

1144
00:56:49.949 --> 00:56:53.953
<i>turning it into the tallest building
in the world!</i>

1145
00:56:55.037 --> 00:56:57.831
<i>And I've put my office right
at the top.</i>

1146
00:56:57.915 --> 00:56:59.583
Now you'll have to look up to me,

1147
00:56:59.667 --> 00:57:02.378
and I'll always look down on you.

1148
00:57:02.461 --> 00:57:03.754
(LAUGHING)

1149
00:57:05.130 --> 00:57:06.924
#Humdinger!

1150
00:57:07.049 --> 00:57:08.550
- (MEOWING)
- (CAMERA SHUTTERS CLICKING)

1151
00:57:09.093 --> 00:57:10.386
(WHIRRING)

1152
00:57:14.306 --> 00:57:15.849
(CRACKLING)

1153
00:57:16.267 --> 00:57:17.893
(ALARM BEEPING)

1154
00:57:19.186 --> 00:57:20.437
(CLANKING)

1155
00:57:22.064 --> 00:57:23.232
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

1156
00:57:24.650 --> 00:57:26.902
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1157
00:57:36.662 --> 00:57:38.038
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

1158
00:57:38.497 --> 00:57:39.915
Oh, no!

1159
00:57:40.374 --> 00:57:41.834
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

1160
00:57:42.918 --> 00:57:44.211
(SCREAMING)

1161
00:57:45.963 --> 00:57:48.090
<i>Marty Muckraker reporting live</i>

1162
00:57:48.173 --> 00:57:50.634
<i>with a correction to this morning's
weather forecast.</i>

1163
00:57:50.718 --> 00:57:53.053
<i>Instead of clear blue skies
and gentle breeze,</i>

1164
00:57:53.178 --> 00:57:56.432
<i>it will now be pitch-black skies
and hurricane-force winds.</i>

1165
00:57:56.807 --> 00:57:58.058
<i>Whoa!</i>

1166
00:57:58.475 --> 00:57:59.518
<i>This just in.</i>

1167
00:57:59.852 --> 00:58:02.354
<i>I've been lying about my hair!</i>

1168
00:58:02.438 --> 00:58:03.772
(THUNDER CRASHING)

1169
00:58:05.524 --> 00:58:07.818
Yikes, that's looking gnarly.

1170
00:58:08.485 --> 00:58:10.696
- (THUNDER CRASHING)
- Ahhh! Ahhh!

1171
00:58:11.071 --> 00:58:12.906
- Rubble!
- What?

1172
00:58:13.157 --> 00:58:15.242
Lightning is frightening!

1173
00:58:15.326 --> 00:58:16.452
(PHONE RINGING)

1174
00:58:16.827 --> 00:58:18.662
PAW Patrol. What's your emergency?

1175
00:58:18.954 --> 00:58:20.456
<i>What's the emergency?</i>

1176
00:58:20.539 --> 00:58:24.418
<i>The mesoscale convective system is
causing exponential thermal lift</i>

1177
00:58:24.501 --> 00:58:28.172
<i>and catastrophic downbursts
at over 190 knots!</i>

1178
00:58:28.589 --> 00:58:29.757
ALL: What?

1179
00:58:30.132 --> 00:58:31.633
It's a super bad storm.

1180
00:58:31.759 --> 00:58:33.719
Come on, guys, keep up.

1181
00:58:33.802 --> 00:58:36.305
<i>Finally, somebody gets me!</i>

1182
00:58:36.513 --> 00:58:38.891
<i>This is not a regular storm.</i>

1183
00:58:39.141 --> 00:58:40.934
<i>It's being caused by
a weather-control device</i>

1184
00:58:41.018 --> 00:58:44.104
<i>that's unleashing
weeks' worth of bad weather all at once!</i>

1185
00:58:44.313 --> 00:58:46.106
Take cover. We're on our way.

1186
00:58:48.567 --> 00:58:50.110
(THUNDER ROARING)

1187
00:58:50.527 --> 00:58:51.820
(ENGINE STARTING)

1188
00:58:52.112 --> 00:58:53.405
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Chase...</i>

1189
00:58:53.489 --> 00:58:56.116
<i>Ready for launch. Go!</i>

1190
00:58:56.742 --> 00:58:57.743
(SIREN BLARING)

1191
00:59:00.162 --> 00:59:02.373
<i>Marshall. Go!</i>

1192
00:59:02.581 --> 00:59:03.999
(SIRENS BLARING)

1193
00:59:05.459 --> 00:59:06.794
(BEEPING)

1194
00:59:07.002 --> 00:59:09.171
<i>Rubble. Go!</i>

1195
00:59:09.254 --> 00:59:10.381
(HONKING)

1196
00:59:11.882 --> 00:59:14.301
<i>Rocky. Go!</i>

1197
00:59:14.802 --> 00:59:16.387
(HOWLING)

1198
00:59:20.766 --> 00:59:21.809
(LAUGHING)

1199
00:59:21.892 --> 00:59:22.976
Whoo-hoo!

1200
00:59:23.060 --> 00:59:24.853
<i>Zuma. Go!</i>

1201
00:59:31.985 --> 00:59:33.028
(SIGHS)

1202
00:59:33.112 --> 00:59:34.822
Go get 'em, pups!

1203
00:59:40.869 --> 00:59:42.496
You know, Liberty,
I've been thinking.

1204
00:59:42.579 --> 00:59:45.582
You're kind of like an honorary member
of the PAW Patrol, right?

1205
00:59:45.999 --> 00:59:48.043
I suppose you could say that.

1206
00:59:48.127 --> 00:59:50.421
I mean, your words, not mine.

1207
00:59:50.838 --> 00:59:54.007
But to be an official member,
you'd need a faster vehicle, right?

1208
00:59:54.216 --> 00:59:55.300
(SIGHING)

1209
00:59:55.384 --> 00:59:56.385
I know, I know,

1210
00:59:56.468 --> 00:59:59.179
my ride's a rusty old wagon
with a wonky wheel

1211
00:59:59.263 --> 01:00:01.140
that goes
"eee-ooo-eee-ooo-eee-ooo."

1212
01:00:01.223 --> 01:00:02.641
You don't have to rub it in.

1213
01:00:03.058 --> 01:00:04.351
- (ENGINE REVVING)
- (GASPS)

1214
01:00:06.186 --> 01:00:08.105
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1215
01:00:11.567 --> 01:00:12.609
(GASPS)

1216
01:00:12.693 --> 01:00:13.694
Is that...

1217
01:00:13.819 --> 01:00:15.154
It's yours.

1218
01:00:15.946 --> 01:00:18.532
Okay, Liberty,
play it cool, play it cool.

1219
01:00:19.199 --> 01:00:21.702
Ahhh! This is amazing! It's the greatest
thing I've ever seen in my life!

1220
01:00:21.785 --> 01:00:22.953
I've never been so happy!

1221
01:00:23.036 --> 01:00:25.080
It's like my whole life has been
building towards this moment!

1222
01:00:25.164 --> 01:00:26.373
All my dreams have come true!

1223
01:00:26.623 --> 01:00:27.749
(MOANING)

1224
01:00:27.833 --> 01:00:30.294
- It's so amazing!
- (LAUGHS)

1225
01:00:35.299 --> 01:00:36.758
(ENGINE REVVING)

1226
01:00:39.428 --> 01:00:41.138
Looking good, Liberty.

1227
01:00:41.972 --> 01:00:44.141
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Liberty!
Ready for launch.</i>

1228
01:00:44.224 --> 01:00:45.517
(GASPS) The voice said my name!

1229
01:00:45.601 --> 01:00:47.561
I can't believe
this is really happening!

1230
01:00:47.853 --> 01:00:49.563
<i>Five...</i>

1231
01:00:50.481 --> 01:00:53.233
<i>Four... Three...</i>

1232
01:00:53.317 --> 01:00:55.319
Wait, I'm not sure I'm ready for this.

1233
01:00:55.402 --> 01:00:57.279
<i>- Two...</i>
- You might want to hang on.

1234
01:00:57.362 --> 01:00:59.656
<i>One... Go!</i>

1235
01:00:59.865 --> 01:01:01.200
(SCREAMING)

1236
01:01:05.412 --> 01:01:06.788
(SCREAMING)

1237
01:01:07.372 --> 01:01:09.041
<i>That's my girl</i>

1238
01:01:09.124 --> 01:01:10.918
<i>That's my girl</i>

1239
01:01:11.585 --> 01:01:13.378
<i>That's my girl</i>

1240
01:01:13.921 --> 01:01:15.631
<i>That's my girl</i>

1241
01:01:15.714 --> 01:01:18.258
<i>What you waiting for</i>

1242
01:01:18.759 --> 01:01:20.594
<i>That's my girl</i>

1243
01:01:20.928 --> 01:01:22.387
Whoo-hoo!

1244
01:01:22.971 --> 01:01:25.265
<i>That's my girl</i>

1245
01:01:26.600 --> 01:01:28.769
- Yeah, Liberty!
- Nice wheels!

1246
01:01:28.852 --> 01:01:30.270
SKYE: Welcome to the team!

1247
01:01:30.354 --> 01:01:32.356
I can't wait to do that again!

1248
01:01:32.439 --> 01:01:33.524
(PUPS LAUGHING)

1249
01:01:33.607 --> 01:01:36.443
Okay, team, we've got no idea
what we're heading into.

1250
01:01:36.527 --> 01:01:38.529
We're going to have to improvise.

1251
01:01:39.905 --> 01:01:41.990
<i>That's my girl</i>

1252
01:01:42.491 --> 01:01:44.868
<i>That's my girl</i>

1253
01:01:45.202 --> 01:01:46.662
(CREAKING)

1254
01:01:49.748 --> 01:01:51.792
Closing in on Humdinger Heights!

1255
01:01:57.548 --> 01:01:58.632
Ugh!

1256
01:01:58.715 --> 01:02:00.717
Things are getting
pretty hairy out here!

1257
01:02:00.801 --> 01:02:04.096
Rocky, Marshall, Rubble,
get those people inside!

1258
01:02:04.179 --> 01:02:06.640
Zuma, Liberty, make sure
the streets are clear.

1259
01:02:06.723 --> 01:02:08.267
Aye aye, Ryder!

1260
01:02:10.435 --> 01:02:11.853
- SKYE: Incoming!
- Look out!

1261
01:02:12.312 --> 01:02:13.647
Arf! Net!

1262
01:02:15.232 --> 01:02:16.525
(GASPING)

1263
01:02:18.860 --> 01:02:20.320
Nice catch!

1264
01:02:20.404 --> 01:02:22.030
You can count on me, Ryder.

1265
01:02:22.531 --> 01:02:24.449
The Cloud Catcher has gone critical.

1266
01:02:24.575 --> 01:02:26.660
There's no way to bring it down!

1267
01:02:26.743 --> 01:02:29.913
- We'll see about that.
- Be careful up there.

1268
01:02:29.997 --> 01:02:31.623
Don't worry about me.

1269
01:02:31.707 --> 01:02:33.917
I can handle a little turbulence.

1270
01:02:41.717 --> 01:02:45.220
Zuma, this is Liberty.
Streets are empty, everyone's safe.

1271
01:02:45.345 --> 01:02:47.723
ZUMA: <i>Copy that. Good job, Liberty!</i>

1272
01:02:50.225 --> 01:02:52.144
- MAN: Help!
- Hold on!

1273
01:02:52.227 --> 01:02:53.353
There's a car in the water.

1274
01:02:53.437 --> 01:02:54.980
I'm diving in!

1275
01:02:55.063 --> 01:02:57.357
<i>Everybody needs somebody sometimes</i>

1276
01:02:57.441 --> 01:02:58.442
Arf! Submarine!

1277
01:02:59.234 --> 01:03:01.903
<i>Everybody needs somebody sometimes</i>

1278
01:03:03.155 --> 01:03:04.698
<i>Everybody needs somebody sometimes</i>

1279
01:03:04.781 --> 01:03:06.408
- Help!
- Help!

1280
01:03:07.159 --> 01:03:08.660
I'm right behind you, Zuma!

1281
01:03:08.744 --> 01:03:10.120
ZUMA: <i>Copy that!</i>

1282
01:03:13.457 --> 01:03:15.709
I'm in your raft, headed downstream.

1283
01:03:18.295 --> 01:03:20.297
ZUMA: I'm closing in on the car.

1284
01:03:24.092 --> 01:03:25.344
Gotcha!

1285
01:03:26.136 --> 01:03:27.679
Arf! Scuba suit!

1286
01:03:28.680 --> 01:03:30.349
<i>Now we just rollin'</i>

1287
01:03:30.432 --> 01:03:32.100
<i>Yeah, we keep it goin'</i>

1288
01:03:32.851 --> 01:03:34.645
It's the PAW Patrol!

1289
01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:36.688
Everybody say cheese!

1290
01:03:36.855 --> 01:03:38.482
- ZUMA: Cheese!
- Hi!

1291
01:03:38.565 --> 01:03:40.692
- Now is not the time for selfies!
- (SIGHING)

1292
01:03:41.360 --> 01:03:42.986
<i>Everybody needs somebody sometimes</i>

1293
01:03:43.195 --> 01:03:45.405
Okay, the rescue raft is in position!

1294
01:03:46.948 --> 01:03:48.283
(ALL GASPING)

1295
01:03:50.952 --> 01:03:52.412
Ryder, this is Zuma!

1296
01:03:52.496 --> 01:03:54.581
The family is safe
and we're headed to dry land.

1297
01:03:54.665 --> 01:03:56.083
RYDER: <i>Good job, pups!</i>

1298
01:03:57.209 --> 01:03:58.794
(THUNDER CRASHING)

1299
01:03:59.503 --> 01:04:00.921
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1300
01:04:01.004 --> 01:04:03.965
You have to get out
of the street right now! It's not safe!

1301
01:04:04.091 --> 01:04:05.550
The mayor is up there!

1302
01:04:07.052 --> 01:04:09.596
I'll get Humdinger.
You get her to safety.

1303
01:04:12.432 --> 01:04:15.686
- Everybody inside!
- This way!

1304
01:04:16.061 --> 01:04:17.479
Follow me!

1305
01:04:17.562 --> 01:04:19.022
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

1306
01:04:19.231 --> 01:04:20.607
- (BANGING)
- Ahhh!

1307
01:04:20.691 --> 01:04:22.818
Everybody, stay away from the windows!

1308
01:04:23.360 --> 01:04:26.571
Hey! That's my hair!
Where did you find it?

1309
01:04:26.655 --> 01:04:29.491
The hair found me.
It was my destiny.

1310
01:04:29.574 --> 01:04:32.786
(GRUNTS) Well, it's my signature look!

1311
01:04:32.994 --> 01:04:34.705
- Buy your own hair!
- (DOOR OPENING)

1312
01:04:36.832 --> 01:04:37.958
(DINGING)

1313
01:04:41.962 --> 01:04:43.213
(BEEPING)

1314
01:04:43.296 --> 01:04:45.340
Cloud Catcher, dead ahead!

1315
01:04:45.841 --> 01:04:48.260
This is gonna get bumpy.

1316
01:04:55.642 --> 01:04:56.852
(THUNDER CRACKLING)

1317
01:04:58.437 --> 01:04:59.604
(MEOWING)

1318
01:05:03.567 --> 01:05:04.901
It's okay, kitties,

1319
01:05:04.985 --> 01:05:07.320
we'll just hunker down
and ride out the storm.

1320
01:05:07.612 --> 01:05:08.822
(ELEVATOR DINGING)

1321
01:05:10.407 --> 01:05:14.202
- Mayor Humdinger?
- Yes? How can I help you?

1322
01:05:14.828 --> 01:05:17.539
- Ryder? What are you doing here?
- (CATS HISSING)

1323
01:05:17.622 --> 01:05:20.709
This tower isn't safe.
We've got to get you out of here.

1324
01:05:22.169 --> 01:05:25.797
Oh, no, the power's out.
That means the elevator's dead.

1325
01:05:25.881 --> 01:05:27.382
We have to go now.

1326
01:05:27.924 --> 01:05:30.594
Nice try! I'm not going
anywhere with you.

1327
01:05:32.679 --> 01:05:35.015
Ah! Oh! Ahhh!

1328
01:05:35.515 --> 01:05:36.558
My top hat!

1329
01:05:37.809 --> 01:05:39.603
Okay, fine. I'll go with you.

1330
01:05:40.353 --> 01:05:41.521
(SQUEALING)

1331
01:05:42.606 --> 01:05:45.734
But I want to make it very clear,
this is not a rescue.

1332
01:05:45.817 --> 01:05:48.945
It's... Uh, an "assisted exit."

1333
01:05:49.112 --> 01:05:50.489
You can call it whatever you want,

1334
01:05:50.572 --> 01:05:52.532
as long as you get in the elevator now!

1335
01:05:52.824 --> 01:05:54.910
I'll release the cables
manually from above.

1336
01:05:54.993 --> 01:05:58.580
Once I've lowered you down safely,
I'll rappel down the elevator shaft.

1337
01:05:59.164 --> 01:06:00.373
Hmpf. Show off.

1338
01:06:00.457 --> 01:06:03.084
Even though we've had
our personal differences over the years,

1339
01:06:03.210 --> 01:06:05.003
I take no pleasure in doing this.

1340
01:06:05.086 --> 01:06:06.087
Doing what?

1341
01:06:06.338 --> 01:06:07.631
Ahhh!

1342
01:06:08.882 --> 01:06:09.883
(LAUGHING)

1343
01:06:09.966 --> 01:06:12.093
Actually, that's pretty satisfying.

1344
01:06:12.803 --> 01:06:17.015
One one thousand, two one thousand,
three one thousand, four one thousand,

1345
01:06:17.098 --> 01:06:18.099
five one thousand.

1346
01:06:18.183 --> 01:06:19.184
(GRUNTS)

1347
01:06:21.228 --> 01:06:22.437
(CONTINUES SCREAMING)

1348
01:06:26.358 --> 01:06:27.609
(ELEVATOR DINGING)

1349
01:06:27.901 --> 01:06:28.985
Oh, uh...

1350
01:06:29.069 --> 01:06:31.363
Nothing to worry about,
everything's fine.

1351
01:06:34.032 --> 01:06:36.952
Okay, pups, Humdinger's out!
I'm coming down.

1352
01:06:37.285 --> 01:06:40.163
<i>Nice job, Ryder! See you on the ground.</i>

1353
01:06:42.082 --> 01:06:43.542
(GRUNTS) Whoa!

1354
01:06:44.042 --> 01:06:45.210
That's not good.

1355
01:06:46.127 --> 01:06:47.879
That's very not good!

1356
01:06:52.008 --> 01:06:53.218
Ahhh! Oh!

1357
01:06:53.301 --> 01:06:54.302
Whoa!

1358
01:06:54.553 --> 01:06:55.846
(CREAKING)

1359
01:06:56.012 --> 01:06:57.764
(SCREAMING)

1360
01:07:00.433 --> 01:07:01.726
(CREAKING)

1361
01:07:09.067 --> 01:07:10.068
(GASPS)

1362
01:07:10.902 --> 01:07:12.028
Ryder!

1363
01:07:27.210 --> 01:07:28.670
Arf! Shields!

1364
01:07:31.882 --> 01:07:33.049
(SIREN BLARING)

1365
01:07:35.135 --> 01:07:36.386
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1366
01:07:40.891 --> 01:07:42.267
Arf! Motorcycle!

1367
01:07:56.865 --> 01:07:58.074
Suction tires!

1368
01:08:02.078 --> 01:08:03.496
I'm coming, Ryder!

1369
01:08:25.644 --> 01:08:27.020
(THUNDER CRASHING)

1370
01:08:28.355 --> 01:08:31.524
Ryder? Ryder? Where are you?

1371
01:08:32.943 --> 01:08:34.152
(BEEPING)

1372
01:08:34.235 --> 01:08:36.821
Ryder! I can see your light. Hang on!

1373
01:08:37.155 --> 01:08:38.365
(PANTING)

1374
01:08:42.535 --> 01:08:43.745
(GASPING)

1375
01:08:54.839 --> 01:08:56.299
I can do this.

1376
01:08:56.591 --> 01:08:57.801
I can do this.

1377
01:08:58.551 --> 01:08:59.928
I can do this!

1378
01:09:00.512 --> 01:09:02.138
Arf! Grappling hook!

1379
01:09:07.227 --> 01:09:08.478
Oh, no!

1380
01:09:11.481 --> 01:09:12.482
(GRUNTS)

1381
01:09:14.526 --> 01:09:15.819
(SCREAMING)

1382
01:09:18.029 --> 01:09:19.364
Disconnect pup pack.

1383
01:09:20.573 --> 01:09:21.825
(SIGHING)

1384
01:09:23.326 --> 01:09:24.494
(GRUNTS)

1385
01:09:30.959 --> 01:09:32.002
Ryder...

1386
01:09:37.465 --> 01:09:41.219
RYDER: <i>I chose you because
you were the bravest pup I'd ever seen.</i>

1387
01:09:44.597 --> 01:09:45.890
(SCREAMING)

1388
01:09:48.018 --> 01:09:50.020
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

1389
01:09:57.318 --> 01:09:58.486
(THUNDER CRASHING)

1390
01:10:05.577 --> 01:10:06.703
(GRUNTS)

1391
01:10:06.786 --> 01:10:08.121
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1392
01:10:10.373 --> 01:10:11.499
Ryder!

1393
01:10:13.960 --> 01:10:15.170
(COUGHING)

1394
01:10:18.131 --> 01:10:19.507
Ryder?

1395
01:10:20.341 --> 01:10:21.468
Chase!

1396
01:10:22.093 --> 01:10:24.387
I can't believe you found me!

1397
01:10:24.763 --> 01:10:27.348
You can always count on me, Ryder.

1398
01:10:27.891 --> 01:10:29.434
- (ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)
- (GASPS)

1399
01:10:29.517 --> 01:10:31.478
Come on, we gotta get out of here!

1400
01:10:31.603 --> 01:10:33.521
I can't. I'm stuck.

1401
01:10:33.813 --> 01:10:36.524
- (COUGHING)
- On three, pull as hard as you can.

1402
01:10:36.733 --> 01:10:39.360
One, two, three!

1403
01:10:39.611 --> 01:10:40.695
(GRUNTING)

1404
01:10:40.779 --> 01:10:42.447
Come on!

1405
01:10:43.656 --> 01:10:44.991
It won't budge.

1406
01:10:46.993 --> 01:10:48.286
One more try.

1407
01:10:48.870 --> 01:10:50.163
(GRUNTING)

1408
01:11:00.924 --> 01:11:02.092
You did it!

1409
01:11:03.176 --> 01:11:04.552
We did it.

1410
01:11:05.762 --> 01:11:07.680
I told you
you were a hero.

1411
01:11:07.764 --> 01:11:09.516
Now come on. Let's get out of here.

1412
01:11:10.767 --> 01:11:12.060
(THUNDER CRASHING)

1413
01:11:16.314 --> 01:11:17.982
Just a little bit further.

1414
01:11:21.778 --> 01:11:23.196
Whoa.

1415
01:11:28.993 --> 01:11:30.703
Oh, great. Lightning.

1416
01:11:30.954 --> 01:11:32.247
(LIGHTNING CRACKLING)

1417
01:11:34.916 --> 01:11:36.126
Arf! Net!

1418
01:11:39.921 --> 01:11:41.256
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Target acquired.</i>

1419
01:11:41.673 --> 01:11:42.841
Fire!

1420
01:11:44.717 --> 01:11:46.094
Got it!

1421
01:11:48.054 --> 01:11:49.097
Whoa!

1422
01:11:49.180 --> 01:11:50.515
Don't got it!

1423
01:11:50.598 --> 01:11:51.766
(SCREAMING)

1424
01:11:51.850 --> 01:11:54.477
AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Warning. Warning. Warning.</i>

1425
01:11:54.561 --> 01:11:56.479
Come on, baby, turn it around!

1426
01:11:59.149 --> 01:12:00.191
(GRUNTS)

1427
01:12:01.151 --> 01:12:02.318
(LIGHTNING CRACKLING)

1428
01:12:10.076 --> 01:12:11.786
Okay, Cloud Catcher...

1429
01:12:11.870 --> 01:12:13.037
Catch this!

1430
01:12:21.379 --> 01:12:22.380
Eject!

1431
01:12:32.432 --> 01:12:33.641
What's that?

1432
01:12:35.393 --> 01:12:38.271
Whoo-hoo! (LAUGHING)

1433
01:12:40.857 --> 01:12:42.609
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1434
01:12:51.367 --> 01:12:54.120
- Yay, Skye!
- Awesome!

1435
01:12:56.831 --> 01:12:58.291
- (LAUGHING)
- Whoa!

1436
01:12:58.917 --> 01:13:00.543
Good job, Skye!

1437
01:13:00.668 --> 01:13:02.337
That was totally awesome!

1438
01:13:02.420 --> 01:13:04.255
You're definitely my favorite pup.

1439
01:13:04.380 --> 01:13:06.966
I hope Ryder got insurance
on my 'copter.

1440
01:13:11.596 --> 01:13:13.097
That'll buff right out.

1441
01:13:18.937 --> 01:13:21.356
- He's okay!
- All right!

1442
01:13:21.439 --> 01:13:23.024
Yeah!

1443
01:13:23.107 --> 01:13:24.234
(LAUGHING)

1444
01:13:24.734 --> 01:13:26.819
Okay, okay. Give him some air.

1445
01:13:29.822 --> 01:13:31.324
- How do you feel?
- (LAUGHING)

1446
01:13:31.908 --> 01:13:33.952
Covered in drool.

1447
01:13:34.035 --> 01:13:36.204
I can't help it, I'm a bulldog.

1448
01:13:36.329 --> 01:13:38.331
My tongue is too big for my mouth!

1449
01:13:38.414 --> 01:13:39.499
See?

1450
01:13:39.582 --> 01:13:40.833
(ALL LAUGHING)

1451
01:13:45.755 --> 01:13:47.298
You did good, pups.

1452
01:13:47.382 --> 01:13:49.884
(PUPS HOWLING)

1453
01:13:49.968 --> 01:13:51.636
(LAUGHING)

1454
01:13:51.719 --> 01:13:53.096
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

1455
01:13:55.598 --> 01:13:57.767
Time for me to get out of here!

1456
01:13:59.227 --> 01:14:01.437
Hey! Mayor Humdinger!

1457
01:14:01.896 --> 01:14:03.231
(MEOWING)

1458
01:14:03.690 --> 01:14:06.234
You are under arrest
for gross negligence,

1459
01:14:06.317 --> 01:14:08.861
public endangerment,
and dog-napping!

1460
01:14:08.987 --> 01:14:11.656
You can't arrest me, I'm the mayor!

1461
01:14:11.781 --> 01:14:13.825
- (LAUGHING)
- (MEOWING)

1462
01:14:13.908 --> 01:14:17.370
- He's getting away!
- Arf! Mini-drone!

1463
01:14:20.290 --> 01:14:21.708
(PANTING)

1464
01:14:26.504 --> 01:14:27.505
Ahhh!

1465
01:14:27.588 --> 01:14:29.716
Hey, hey, hey!

1466
01:14:30.633 --> 01:14:32.385
(SCREAMING)

1467
01:14:33.136 --> 01:14:34.387
Put me down!

1468
01:14:34.512 --> 01:14:37.890
Nobody makes a fool of Mayor Humdinger
five times in the same day!

1469
01:14:37.974 --> 01:14:39.559
Ahhh! (GRUNTS)

1470
01:14:41.311 --> 01:14:42.395
(SHRIEKS)

1471
01:14:42.979 --> 01:14:45.648
Well, this is humiliating.

1472
01:14:45.732 --> 01:14:47.191
Here you go, boss.

1473
01:14:48.067 --> 01:14:49.444
That's better.

1474
01:14:52.697 --> 01:14:54.907
KENDRA: <i>Adventure City is our home.</i>

1475
01:14:55.158 --> 01:14:57.785
<i>It's up to all of us to take care of it.</i>

1476
01:15:03.333 --> 01:15:06.085
<i>But once in a while, a group of heroes</i>

1477
01:15:06.169 --> 01:15:09.213
<i>go above and beyond the call of duty.</i>

1478
01:15:09.422 --> 01:15:11.466
<i>They look out for their neighbors</i>

1479
01:15:11.549 --> 01:15:13.259
<i>before they look out for themselves.</i>

1480
01:15:14.052 --> 01:15:17.764
<i>And they're so darn cute,
I just want to squeeze 'em!</i>

1481
01:15:18.222 --> 01:15:22.226
<i>It is our great honor to present
the key to Adventure City to...</i>

1482
01:15:22.310 --> 01:15:24.270
<i>- The PAW Patrol!</i>
- The PAW Patrol!

1483
01:15:24.354 --> 01:15:25.563
(CROWD CHEERING)

1484
01:15:27.273 --> 01:15:28.983
(EPIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1485
01:15:34.530 --> 01:15:37.658
Me and the PAW Patrol, we go way back!

1486
01:15:38.159 --> 01:15:39.202
(ROOSTER CROWING)

1487
01:15:39.285 --> 01:15:42.830
And to think I knew them
before they were famous!

1488
01:15:43.039 --> 01:15:45.958
Hey, Rubble, I got something for you.

1489
01:15:49.212 --> 01:15:51.672
I am never taking this off!

1490
01:15:51.756 --> 01:15:52.882
(PUPS LAUGHING)

1491
01:15:52.965 --> 01:15:55.718
<i>I want to take this special occasion
to introduce you</i>

1492
01:15:55.802 --> 01:15:57.970
<i>to the newest member
of the PAW Patrol.</i>

1493
01:15:58.054 --> 01:15:59.680
<i>Adventure City's very own...</i>

1494
01:15:59.931 --> 01:16:01.557
<i>Liberty!</i>

1495
01:16:01.641 --> 01:16:02.892
(CROWD CHEERING)

1496
01:16:10.191 --> 01:16:11.859
My own pup tag?

1497
01:16:12.151 --> 01:16:14.028
Welcome to the family, Liberty.

1498
01:16:15.113 --> 01:16:16.322
I'm official.

1499
01:16:16.406 --> 01:16:18.866
Hey, check it out!
I'm officially official!

1500
01:16:19.117 --> 01:16:21.869
Official member
of the PAW Patrol right here!

1501
01:16:22.203 --> 01:16:23.830
(PUPS HOWLING)

1502
01:16:25.081 --> 01:16:26.332
(LIBERTY HOWLS)

1503
01:16:27.291 --> 01:16:28.626
<i>Thank you for this honor.</i>

1504
01:16:28.751 --> 01:16:32.130
<i>The PAW Patrol will always
look out for Adventure City.</i>

